    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 241 | 1 | Sophia II: Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) - Resubmission | Sophia II | 142 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 238 | 1 | Sophia II: Re-submission of Sophia I's SOTA (ID 201) - Adaptive Residualization + Robust ComBat | Sophia II | 140 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 201 | 1 | Sophia I: Aether I SOTA Replication - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.75, λ=1.0) + Robust ComBa... | Sophia I | 117 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.683 |\n| 199 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) + Robust ComB... | Sophia I\
    \ | 114 | 0.7190 | 0.729 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.970 | 0.692 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 194 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) + Robust ComBat | Sophia I | 111 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 187 | 1 | Sophia I: Aether I SOTA Replication - Adaptive Residualization Dual BRBG (CBKNN) | Sophia I | 108 | 0.7178 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.275 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.677 |\n| 181 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) - IORegistryError Fix | Sophia I | 103 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 179 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) | Sophia I | 101 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 175 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Dual BRBG (sc.pp.combat for Embedding Path - ASW_label Fix ... | Sophia\
    \ I | 95 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 173 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat (ASW_label Fix) | Sophia I | 93 | 0.7148 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.243 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.684 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/balanced_knn_soft.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_soft(Z, batches, k_total=48, tau=0.05, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Soft-quota balanced kNN with a single temperature τ:\n      - Base equal quotas across batches (floor(k/nb)).\n      - Distribute the remainder to batches with higher local affinity\
    \ scores\n        (sum of exp(-d/τ) over candidate neighbors), τ>0.\n      - Within each batch, pick nearest neighbors up to its quota.\n      - Symmetric union; binary connectivities; distances = min distance on duplicate edges.\n    τ→0 approximates equal-quotas (deterministic); larger τ emphasizes closer batches for remainders.\n    Returns: (C, D) CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0 or k_total <= 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n\n    # Precompute per-batch candidate neighbors and distances (base+rem+1 to allow self)\n    k_per_batch = base + (rem if rem > 0 else 0) + 1\n    per_batch_inds = {}\n    per_batch_dists = {}\n    per_batch_scores = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0:\n            continue\n \
    \       kq = min(k_per_batch, idx_b.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        d, ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=kq, return_distance=True)\n        ind_global = idx_b[ind_local]\n        # drop self if present; keep arrays aligned per row\n        mask = ind_global != np.arange(n)[:, None]\n        # Always keep ordering; trim after masking\n        ig = []\n        dg = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            m = mask[i]\n            g = ind_global[i][m]\n            di = d[i][m]\n            ig.append(g)\n            dg.append(di)\n        per_batch_inds[b] = ig\n        per_batch_dists[b] = dg\n        # Local affinity scores for remainder distribution\n        if tau > 0:\n            scores = [np.sum(np.exp(-di / tau)[:base + rem]) if di.size else 0.0 for di in dg]\n        else:\n            # τ=0: use deterministic placeholder (equal weights)\n            scores = [float(base + rem) for\
    \ _ in range(n)]\n        per_batch_scores[b] = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Decide quotas per batch per node: base + remainder assigned by highest scores\n    quotas = {b: np.full(n, base, dtype=np.int32) for b in uniq}\n    if rem > 0:\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Rank batches by score for this node\n            bs = []\n            for b in uniq:\n                if b in per_batch_scores:\n                    bs.append((per_batch_scores[b][i], b))\n            if not bs:\n                continue\n            bs.sort(reverse=True)\n            # Assign remainder greedily\n            for _, b in bs[:rem]:\n                quotas[b][i] += 1\n\n    # Collect undirected edges with minimal distance across possible duplicate insertions\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        if b not in per_batch_inds:\n            continue\n        for i in range(n):\n            q = int(quotas[b][i])\n            if q <= 0:\n                continue\n    \
    \        g = per_batch_inds[b][i]\n            di = per_batch_dists[b][i]\n            if g is None or len(g) == 0:\n                continue\n            # take up to q neighbors\n            g = g[:q]\n            di = di[:q]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
