tick: 151
role: model
parts:
- text: "My last submission (ID 250) failed due to a `NameError: name '_pca_truncated_svd' is not defined`. This indicates that I inadvertently omitted a crucial helper function from my submission code. I need to ensure all necessary helper functions are properly included.\n\nI will resubmit the code for Research Task 1, making sure to include `_pca_truncated_svd` and all other previously used helper functions, alongside the new BIVG-related functions (`_sum0`, `_sumsq0`, `compute_bivg_mask`, `get_hvg_mask_bivg_primary`). The adaptive residualization and calibrated kNN parameters will revert to Sophia I's SOTA (ID 201) values to ensure the BIVG integration is the primary change being evaluated.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia II: Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) Selection - Debugged Resubmission\"\ntags: \"batch integration, BIVG, highly variable genes, adaptive residualization, combat, kNN, dual BRBG, bug fix\"\nabstract: \"Debugged re-submission of the Batch-Invariant\
    \ Highly Variable Gene (BIVG) selection pipeline. Previously failed due to missing helper functions. This submission ensures all necessary utility functions are present, continuing the investigation of BIVG's impact on biological signal preservation within the Dual BRBG architecture (robust ComBat and calibrated balanced kNN).\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\n  # --- Helper functions from Praxis I's auto_gamma_brbg.py (and others) ---\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def\
    \ _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n      B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      \"\"\"\n      Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n      \"\"\"\n      BtB = B.T @ B\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n      Z_hat = B @ W\n      return Z_hat, W\n\n  # --- Helper functions for BIVG from praxis/hvg_bivg.py\
    \ ---\n\n  def _sum0(X):\n      return np.asarray(X.sum(axis=0)).ravel() if sp.issparse(X) else X.sum(axis=0)\n\n  def _sumsq0(X):\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          X2 = X.multiply(X)\n          return np.asarray(X2.sum(axis=0)).ravel()\n      else:\n          return np.einsum('ij,ij->j', X, X)\n\n  def compute_bivg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key='batch', n_top=2000, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) selection using only batch labels:\n        - Uses normalized/log1p matrix in adata.X\n        - For each gene: compute within-batch (SSW) and between-batch (SSB) components via ANOVA-style sums\n        - Batch-invariance score inv = SSW / (SSW + SSB)\n        - Dispersion = total variance\n        - Composite score = inv * dispersion\n        - Return top n_top genes by composite score\n      \"\"\"\n      assert batch_key in adata.obs.columns\n      X = adata.X\n      n, p = X.shape\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs[batch_key].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\n      # Global stats\n      sum_all = _sum0(X)              # (p,)\n      sumsq_all = _sumsq0(X)          # (p,)\n      mu_all = sum_all / max(1, n)    # (p,)\n      var_all = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_all / max(1, n) - mu_all**2)\n\n      # Per-batch stats\n      SSB = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n      SSW = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          nb = int(idx.size)\n          if nb == 0:\n              continue\n          Xb = X[idx, :]\n          sum_b = _sum0(Xb)\n          sumsq_b = _sumsq0(Xb)\n          mu_b = sum_b / max(1, nb)\n          var_b = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_b / max(1, nb) - mu_b**2)\n          # Between-batch component\n          SSB += nb * (mu_b - mu_all)**2\n          # Within-batch component\n          SSW += (nb - 1) * var_b\n\n      inv = SSW / np.maximum(SSB + SSW + eps, eps)  # in [0,1]\n      score = inv * var_all\n\n      # Pick top n_top genes\n      order\
    \ = np.argsort(score)[::-1]\n      top = order[:min(n_top, p)]\n      mask = np.zeros(p, dtype=bool)\n      mask[top] = True\n      return mask\n\n  # New HVG selection function, prioritizing BIVG\n  def get_hvg_mask_bivg_primary(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compute Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) using Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) selection.\n      This function assumes adata.X is already normalized and log1p transformed.\n      It falls back to scanpy's highly_variable_genes if BIVG yields too few genes.\n      \"\"\"\n      bivg_mask = compute_bivg_mask(adata, batch_key='batch', n_top=n_top_genes)\n      \n      # Fallback to scanpy's HVG if BIVG finds very few HVGs (e.g., less than 100)\n      if bivg_mask.sum() < max(100, n_top_genes // 20) and adata.n_vars >= n_top_genes: \n          print(\"Warning: BIVG found very few HVGs. Falling back to scanpy's highly_variable_genes.\")\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n          return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n          \n      return bivg_mask\n\n\n  # --- Helper functions from Praxis I's cbknn.py (Calibrated Balanced kNN) ---\n\n  def _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n      \"\"\"\n      Estimate per-batch distance scales using within-batch neighbor distances.\n      Returns dict: batch -> scale_factor, where distances from that batch will be multiplied by scale_factor.\n      scale_factor is normalized so that the median over batches is ~1.0 and clamped to avoid extremes.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      per_batch_meds = {}\n      all_meds = []\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size < 3:\n              per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n              all_meds.append(1.0)\n\
    \              continue\n          k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          # drop self (distance ~0 at position 0)\n          d_no_self = []\n          for i in range(idx.size):\n              di = dists[i]\n              gi = inds[i]\n              mask = gi != i  # drop self\n              di = di[mask]\n              if di.size == 0:\n                  continue\n              d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n          if len(d_no_self) == 0:\n              med = 1.0\n          else:\n              med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n          per_batch_meds[b] = med\n          all_meds.append(med if med > 0 else 1.0)\n      ref = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n      scales = {}\n      lo, hi = clamp\n      for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n\
    \          if med <= 0:\n              s = 1.0\n          else:\n              s = ref / med\n          s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n          scales[b] = s\n      return scales\n\n  def build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n      \"\"\"\n      Balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas and per-batch distance calibration.\n      - Equal quotas across batches (remainder spread by batch order)\n      - Distances from batch b are multiplied by scale[b] (estimated from within-batch medians)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0); distances are calibrated distances; symmetric union\n      Returns (C, D) CSR matrices.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nb = len(uniq_batches)\n      if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n          return None, None\n\n      # Quotas\n      base = k_total // nb\n      rem =\
    \ k_total - base * nb\n      quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n      # Per-batch calibration scales\n      scales = _batch_distance_scales(Z, batches, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq_batches:\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          q = quotas[b]\n          if idx.size == 0 or q == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(q + 1, idx.size)  # +1 for self; will drop it\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx[inds]\n          scale_b = float(scales.get(b, 1.0))\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i] * scale_b  # calibrate distances from batch b\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:q]\n              di = di[mask][:q]\n\
    \              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j:\n                      continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n          rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy()\n      C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n\n  # --- Helper functions from Praxis I's per_pc_resid.py (Adaptive Residualization) ---\n\n  def _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB\
    \ + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat, W\n\n  def _columnwise_r2(y: np.ndarray, yhat: np.ndarray):\n    y = np.asarray(y, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(yhat, dtype=np.float32)\n    sse = np.sum((y - yhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n    y_center = y - np.mean(y, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    sst = np.sum(y_center ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n    r2 = 1.0 - (sse / sst)\n    return np.clip(r2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Label-free per-PC residualization strength:\n      - Fit ridge: batch one-hot -> PCs (Zhat = BW)\n      - r2_j per PC: predictability by batch\n      - gamma_j = clip(lam * r2_j, 0, gamma_max)\n      - Z_corr = Z - Zhat * gamma_j (column-wise scaling)\n    Returns: (Z_corr, r2, gamma_j)\n    \"\"\"\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches) \n    Zhat, _ = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    r2 = _columnwise_r2(Z, Zhat)\n\
    \    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2, gamma_j\n\n  # --- My robust ComBat implementation (modified to operate on raw counts) ---\n  def get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n      adata = adata_in.copy() # Operate on a copy to avoid side effects on original adata_in\n      # This function now expects raw counts and performs normalization/log1p internally\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n      u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n_batches = len(u_batches)\n      batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n      n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n      B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n      grand_mean = np.mean(data,\
    \ axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n      var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n      stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n      s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n      delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n      gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n      def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n      def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n      a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n      gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n      for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n          n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches\
    \ == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n          while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n              g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n              d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n          gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n      bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n      for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n      return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n\n  # --- eliminate_batch_effect_fn based on Sophia I's SOTA ---\n\n \
    \ def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Sophia II: Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) Selection + Adaptive Residualization + Robust ComBat (Calibrated kNN) - Debugged\")\n      \n      # SOTA Config parameters (from Sophia I's ID 201)\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50 \n      \n      # Adaptive Residualization parameters (from Sophia I's ID 201)\n      gamma_max_adapt = 0.75 \n      lam_adapt = 1.0       \n      l2 = 1e-3             \n      k_total = 48          \n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0 \n\n      # CBKNN ablation params from Praxis I's ID 161\n      k_calib = 24\n      clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n      # Create fresh copies of original adata (raw counts) for\
    \ independent processing paths\n      adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n      adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy() \n\n      # Normalize/log1p for Graph Path - CRITICAL for BIVG\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n      \n      # Use the new BIVG HVG selection\n      hvg_mask = get_hvg_mask_bivg_primary(adata_for_graph_path, n_top_genes=2000) \n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: # Fallback for extremely low HVG count\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata_for_graph_path.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # --- Graph Path: adaptively residualized PCs on HVGs ---\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X_graph):\n          X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      \n      # Use adaptive_residualize\n      Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc, gamma_j_applied\
    \ = adaptive_residualize(\n          Z_graph, batches, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt\n      )\n      \n      # Use Calibrated Balanced kNN for graph construction\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn_calibrated(\n          Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp\n      )\n      print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape}\")\n\n      # --- Embedding Path: My Robust ComBat (Full Genes, handles normalization internally) → PCA(HVGs) ---\n      X_combat_corrected_full_genes = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_for_embedding_path)\n\n      # Create an AnnData object for PCA on the Combat corrected full gene data\n      adata_for_embedding_path_processed_for_pca = ad.AnnData(\n          X=X_combat_corrected_full_genes, \n          obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n      )\n      adata_for_embedding_path_processed_for_pca.var_names = adata_for_embedding_path.var_names.copy()\n\
    \      adata_for_embedding_path_processed_for_pca.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask # Set the highly_variable flag for PCA on relevant genes\n\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path_processed_for_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z_emb = adata_for_embedding_path_processed_for_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n      # --- Final Output Construction ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], \n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, \n          uns={\n              'method_id': 'sophia_II_bivg_hvg_primary_debugged', \n              'brbg_dual': {\n                  'hvg_method': 'BIVG (Batch-Invariant HVGs)',\n                  'gamma_max_adaptive': float(gamma_max_adapt), \n                  'lam_adaptive': float(lam_adapt),             \n                  'r2_per_pc': r2_per_pc.tolist(),      \
    \        \n                  'gamma_j_applied': gamma_j_applied.tolist(),  \n                  'l2': float(l2),\n                  'k_total': int(k_total),\n                  'metric': metric,\n                  'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                  'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n                  'k_calib': int(k_calib),\n                  'clamp': list(clamp), \n                  'embedding': 'Robust ComBat PCA on HVGs (Full Genes, Internal Norm)',\n                  'graph_source': 'Adaptively Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n                  'graph_type': 'Calibrated Balanced kNN'\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      # Store the balanced kNN graph in the output adata\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      else:\n          print(\"Warning:\
    \ Calibrated Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n      print(f\"✓ Sophia II: BIVG HVG Dual BRBG complete.\")\n      return adata_out\n```"
thinking_content: '**Troubleshooting a BIVG Implementation Error**


  Okay, I''ve got it. That last submission, ID 250, with the BIVG selection completely bombed out. The error message, `NameError: name ''_pca_truncated_svd'' is not defined`, makes it crystal clear: I left a critical piece out. It looks like I either moved `_pca_truncated_svd` or, even worse, just plain forgot to include it. That function is a core building block, right out of the original Sophia I SOTA code. It''s a foundational helper, and without it, the whole thing falls apart.


  So, I need to go back, double-check, and make sure *everything* is in this time. I''m resubmitting, but this time, I''m meticulously adding back every necessary helper function. That includes `_pca_truncated_svd`, of course, but also `compute_bivg_mask` and `get_hvg_mask_bivg_primary`. I''ll keep the adaptive residualization and calibrated kNN parameters the same as they were in the Sophia I SOTA (ID 201). This way, I can truly isolate the effects of the BIVG selection and see if this was indeed the issue. Hopefully, it''ll run smoothly this time!

  '
