  Alright, so submission ID 279 is chugging along, and I''m itching to see the results. My gut feeling, after reflecting on the previous runs, is that a more balanced approach – playing with the `adv_weight`, cranking up the `latent_dim`, going deeper with the networks, and maybe giving the discriminator a slightly faster learning rate – will finally stabilize this BC-VAE training. Hopefully, this combo will allow for better batch correction without throwing the biological signal out the window.


