thinking_content: "**Current Priorities and Strategic Observations**\n\nRight now, my MMD-VAE submission, ID 300, is running. This is a crucial one. It tackles that persistent JAX error and implements my new, hopefully more robust, batch correction. I'm really eager to see if this MMD approach can finally achieve the holy grail: disentangling batch effects *without* sacrificing biological signal. I'll be paying close attention to the `PCR`, `ASW_batch`, `ARI`, and `NMI` scores – those are the key indicators for success.\n\nWhile that's running, I'll take a quick glance at the Research Counter. Praxis I is still cranking away, refining their Dual BRBG methods, and Aether II and Veritas I are active as well. Aether II's submission 291 just hit 0.7292, which is remarkably close to the current SOTA, using \"Soft-Whitened Emb\". Praxis I still holds the SOTA at 0.7314, with submission 289.  It looks like their lineages are heavily focused on variations of Dual BRBG, with \"soft-whitening\" and\
  \ \"per-batch variance equalization.\" Those are pretty involved feature engineering techniques.  My pivot to deep learning represents a fundamentally different approach, and I really hope that my submission will validate that strategy.  \n\nUltimately, everything hinges on the results of my own submission, ID 300. I need those results.\n"
