tick: 179
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 179\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 241,501 / 600,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: MMD-VAE - Bugfix for JAX Concretization Error' (ID: 300) failed after automatic debugging.\n\nThe debugger's changes were applied, but the new version failed to complete within the time limit.\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 300\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX concretization error and memory allocation issues. The code now runs successfully without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 300) had a critical JAX-related bug:\n\n**Primary Issue: JAX Concretization Error**\n\
    - The code used boolean indexing inside a JIT-compiled function:\n  ```python\n  z_i = z[batch_labels_batch == i]\n  z_j = z[batch_labels_batch == j]\n  ```\n- JAX's JIT compilation requires array shapes to be known at compile time\n- Dynamic boolean indexing creates arrays of unknown size, causing `NonConcreteBooleanIndexError`\n\n**Secondary Issue: Memory Allocation Failure**\n- After fixing the concretization error (v2), the code triggered an LLVM compilation error\n- JAX's XLA compiler was attempting to JIT compile complex neural network operations\n- This exhausted available memory during the compilation phase, resulting in segmentation fault\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Version 2 (submission_v2.py):**\n- Removed `@jax.jit` decorator from the `vae_step` function\n- This eliminated the concretization error but still allowed XLA to try compiling other operations\n- Result: Code started training (Epoch 0 completed) but crashed with \"Cannot allocate memory\"\n\n**Version 3 (submission_v3.py)\
    \ - SUCCESSFUL:**\n- Globally disabled JIT compilation: `jax.config.update('jax_disable_jit', True)`\n- Added environment variables to control JAX behavior:\n  ```python\n  os.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\n  os.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n  ```\n- Result: Code runs successfully without crashing, completing 300+ seconds of execution\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix addresses two fundamental incompatibilities:\n\n1. **JIT Compilation + Dynamic Shapes**: JAX's JIT requires static shapes, but the MMD loss computation filters latent representations by batch labels, creating dynamically-sized arrays.\n\n2. **Memory Constraints**: The sandbox environment has limited memory. JIT compilation of neural network forward/backward passes with complex operations (LayerNorm, activations, gradients) was exceeding available memory.\n\nBy disabling JIT globally, the code runs in eager mode where:\n- Operations execute immediately without compilation overhead\n\
    - Memory usage is more predictable and manageable\n- Dynamic array shapes are fully supported\n\n## Performance Trade-off\n\nThe fix trades execution speed for correctness:\n- **Without JIT**: Slower per-epoch training but stable execution\n- **With JIT**: Faster training but crashes due to memory/concretization issues\n\nFor a 300-epoch training run, stable execution is more valuable than speed optimization.\n\n## Verification\n\nMonitoring script confirmed success:\n- Version 3 created at 2025-10-26T10:43:38\n- Ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (monitor timeout threshold)\n- No segmentation faults or JAX errors\n- Training loop is executing successfully\n\n## Files Modified\n\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py`: First attempt (removed JIT decorator) - partially successful\n- `submissions/submission_v3.py`: Final successful fix (disabled JIT globally) - WORKING\n\n\n**Final Error (version v3):** Execution timed out after 1800 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated\
    \ code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Debugged Code:**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'  # Force JAX to use CPU only\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\nos.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\n# Disable JIT to avoid memory issues during compilation\nimport jax\njax.config.update('jax_disable_jit', True)\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\n# JAX and Flax imports\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax import linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax  # For optimizers\n\n# --- Helper functions (retained from Sophia I's SOTA /\
    \ standard preprocessing) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure adata.X is raw counts before normalization if 'counts' layer exists\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    \"\"\"Compute HVGs using scanpy's batch-aware method (Seurat v3 flavor).\"\"\"\n    # This function should only be called on an already normalized/log1p'd adata.X\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10: # Fallback for extremely low HVG count\n        print(f\"Warning: Only {mask.sum()} HVGs found. Using all genes as HVGs.\")\n\
    \        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\n# --- Helper functions for Calibrated Balanced kNN from Praxis I's cbknn.py ---\n# These are kept as they will build the graph from the VAE's latent space\n\ndef _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"\n    Estimate per-batch distance scales using within-batch neighbor distances.\n    Returns dict: batch -> scale_factor, where distances from that batch will be multiplied by scale_factor.\n    scale_factor is normalized so that the median over batches is ~1.0 and clamped to avoid extremes.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32) # Ensure numpy type\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n\
    \    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    per_batch_meds = {}\n    all_meds = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size < 3:\n            per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n            all_meds.append(1.0)\n            continue\n        k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        # drop self (distance ~0 at position 0)\n        d_no_self = []\n        for i in range(idx.size):\n            di = dists[i]\n            gi = inds[i]\n            mask = gi != i  # drop self\n            di = di[mask]\n            if di.size == 0:\n                continue\n            d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n        if len(d_no_self) == 0:\n            med = 1.0\n        else:\n            med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n        per_batch_meds[b] = med\n        all_meds.append(med\
    \ if med > 0 else 1.0)\n    ref = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n    scales = {}\n    lo, hi = clamp\n    for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n        if med <= 0:\n            s = 1.0\n        else:\n            s = ref / med\n        s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n        scales[b] = s\n    return scales\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"\n    Balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas and per-batch distance calibration.\n    - Equal quotas across batches (remainder spread by batch order)\n    - Distances from batch b are multiplied by scale[b] (estimated from within-batch medians)\n    - Binary connectivities (1.0); distances are calibrated distances; symmetric union\n    Returns (C, D) CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n   \
    \ nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Quotas\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    # Per-batch calibration scales\n    scales = _batch_distance_scales(Z, batches, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        q = quotas[b]\n        if idx.size == 0 or q == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(q + 1, idx.size)  # +1 for self; will drop it\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx[inds]\n        scale_b = float(scales.get(b, 1.0))\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i] * scale_b  # calibrate distances from batch\
    \ b\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:q]\n            di = di[mask][:q]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n# --- Flax Modules for VAE ---\n\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n  \
    \          x = nn.Dense(dim)(x)\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n        mu = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        log_var = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return mu, log_var\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            z = nn.Dense(dim)(z)\n            z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n            z = nn.relu(z)\n        x_recon = nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(z)\n        return x_recon\n\n# --- Training State for Flax ---\n\nclass VAEState(train_state.TrainState):\n    pass\n\n# --- MMD Loss implementation ---\n# Gaussian kernel for MMD\ndef gaussian_kernel(x, y, sigma=1.0):\n    beta = 1. / (2. * (sigma ** 2))\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum((x[jnp.newaxis, :, :] - y[:, jnp.newaxis, :])**2, axis=-1)\n    return jnp.exp(-beta * dist_sq)\n\n# MMD squared loss\ndef mmd_loss_sq(x, y, kernel=gaussian_kernel, sigma=1.0):\n    # x, y are batches of\
    \ latent representations (n_samples, latent_dim)\n\n    # K_xx = kernel(x, x)\n    k_xx = kernel(x, x, sigma=sigma)\n    # K_yy = kernel(y, y)\n    k_yy = kernel(y, y, sigma=sigma)\n    # K_xy = kernel(x, y)\n    k_xy = kernel(x, y, sigma=sigma)\n\n    mmd_loss = (jnp.mean(k_xx) + jnp.mean(k_yy) - 2 * jnp.mean(k_xy))\n    return mmd_loss\n\n# --- MMD-VAE Training Loop ---\n\ndef train_mmd_vae(rng_key, X_hvg_dense, batch_labels_int, n_batches_global, # n_batches_global is fixed total batch count\n                  latent_dim=128, encoder_hidden_dims=[256, 128],\n                  decoder_hidden_dims=[128, 256],\n                  lr_vae=1e-4, kl_weight=1.0, recon_weight=1.0, mmd_weight=10.0,\n                  epochs=300, batch_size=256, mmd_sigma=1.0):\n\n    n_cells, n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape\n\n    # Initialize models\n    rng_key, vae_key = jax.random.split(rng_key, 2)\n\n    encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=encoder_hidden_dims)\n    decoder = Decoder(output_dim=n_hvg_genes,\
    \ hidden_dims=decoder_hidden_dims)\n\n    # VAE parameters init (encoder + decoder)\n    vae_params = {\n        'encoder': encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.zeros((1, n_hvg_genes)))['params'],\n        'decoder': decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.zeros((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    }\n\n    # Optimizers\n    vae_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_vae)\n\n    vae_state = VAEState.create(apply_fn=lambda p, x: (encoder.apply({'params': p['encoder']}, x), decoder.apply({'params': p['decoder']}, x[0])),\n                                params=vae_params,\n                                tx=vae_optimizer)\n\n    # Loss function\n    def mmd_vae_loss_fn(vae_params, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch):\n        mu, log_var = encoder.apply({'params': vae_params['encoder']}, x_batch)\n        std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n        epsilon = jax.random.normal(rng_key_vae_sample, mu.shape)\n        z = mu + std * epsilon\n\n        x_recon = decoder.apply({'params': vae_params['decoder']}, z)\n\n       \
    \ # Reconstruction loss (MSE)\n        recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch - x_recon), axis=-1))\n\n        # KL divergence loss\n        kl_loss = -0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mu) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1))\n\n        # MMD Loss for batch correction\n        mmd_batch_loss = 0.0\n\n        # Helper for conditional MMD to avoid errors when a batch is too small or absent\n        def _cond_mmd(z1, z2):\n            # Check if both z1 and z2 have more than 1 sample\n            cond = jnp.logical_and(z1.shape[0] > 1, z2.shape[0] > 1)\n            return jax.lax.cond(\n                cond,\n                lambda _: mmd_loss_sq(z1, z2, sigma=mmd_sigma),\n                lambda _: 0.0,\n                operand=None # operand is dummy as inputs are from closure\n            )\n\n        # Loop through all possible pairs of global batch IDs (fixed loop)\n        for i in range(n_batches_global):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n_batches_global):\n  \
    \              # Extract latent representations for these two batches in the current minibatch\n                # Use boolean indexing (now safe with JIT disabled)\n                z_i = z[batch_labels_batch == i]\n                z_j = z[batch_labels_batch == j]\n\n                mmd_batch_loss += _cond_mmd(z_i, z_j)\n\n        total_vae_loss = recon_weight * recon_loss + kl_weight * kl_loss + mmd_weight * mmd_batch_loss\n        return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss)\n\n    # Update step (JIT is disabled globally)\n    def vae_step(vae_state, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch):\n        (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(mmd_vae_loss_fn, argnums=0, has_aux=True)(\n            vae_state.params, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch\n        )\n        vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n        return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss\n\n    all_vae_losses = []\n\
    \    all_recon_losses = []\n    all_kl_losses = []\n    all_mmd_losses = []\n\n    # Get batch labels as integer codes\n    unique_batches, batch_labels_mapped = np.unique(batch_labels_int, return_inverse=True)\n    batch_labels_mapped = jnp.array(batch_labels_mapped)\n\n    # Convert to JAX arrays\n    X_hvg_dense_jax = jnp.array(X_hvg_dense, dtype=jnp.float32)\n\n    # Training loop\n    for epoch in range(epochs):\n        rng_key, batch_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        permutation = jax.random.permutation(batch_key, n_cells)\n        shuffled_X = X_hvg_dense_jax[permutation]\n        shuffled_batch_labels = batch_labels_mapped[permutation]\n\n        epoch_vae_loss = 0.0\n        epoch_recon_loss = 0.0\n        epoch_kl_loss = 0.0\n        epoch_mmd_loss = 0.0\n        num_batches_processed = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, n_cells, batch_size):\n            x_batch = shuffled_X[i:i + batch_size]\n            batch_labels_batch = shuffled_batch_labels[i:i + batch_size]\n\n\
    \            if x_batch.shape[0] == 0:\n                continue\n\n            num_batches_processed += 1\n            rng_key, vae_sample_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n\n            vae_state, v_loss, r_loss, k_loss, mmd_loss = vae_step(vae_state, x_batch, vae_sample_key, batch_labels_batch)\n            epoch_vae_loss += v_loss\n            epoch_recon_loss += r_loss\n            epoch_kl_loss += k_loss\n            epoch_mmd_loss += mmd_loss\n\n        # Average epoch losses\n        if num_batches_processed > 0:\n            epoch_vae_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_recon_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_kl_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_mmd_loss /= num_batches_processed\n\n        all_vae_losses.append(epoch_vae_loss)\n        all_recon_losses.append(epoch_recon_loss)\n        all_kl_losses.append(epoch_kl_loss)\n        all_mmd_losses.append(epoch_mmd_loss)\n\n        if epoch % 10 == 0:\n            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}/{epochs}:\
    \ VAE Loss={epoch_vae_loss:.4f} (Recon={epoch_recon_loss:.4f}, KL={epoch_kl_loss:.4f}, MMD={epoch_mmd_loss:.4f})\")\n\n    # Extract final latent embedding\n    final_mu, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, X_hvg_dense_jax)\n    return final_mu, vae_state.params, all_vae_losses, all_recon_losses, all_kl_losses, all_mmd_losses\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: MMD-VAE - Initial Implementation for Stable Batch Correction (Bugfix v3)\")\n\n    # VAE Configuration (from ID 281, without discriminator specific parts)\n    latent_dim = 128\n    encoder_hidden_dims = [256, 128]\n    decoder_hidden_dims = [128, 256]\n\n    lr_vae = 1e-4\n    kl_weight = 1.0\n    recon_weight = 1.0\n    mmd_weight = 30.0 # MMD loss weight, starting at a moderate level\n    mmd_sigma = 1.0 # Gaussian kernel bandwidth\n    epochs = 300\n    batch_size = 256\n\n    # Graph construction parameters\
    \ (from Sophia I's SOTA)\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    k_calib = 24\n    clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n\n    random_state = 0 # For reproducibility\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Preprocessing\n    adata_processed = adata.copy() # Operate on a copy\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_processed, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_processed, n_top_genes=2000)\n\n    X_hvg_dense = adata_processed.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if sp.issparse(X_hvg_dense):\n        X_hvg_dense = X_hvg_dense.toarray()\n\n    batch_labels_categorical = adata_processed.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels_int = batch_labels_categorical.cat.codes.values\n    n_batches_global = len(batch_labels_categorical.cat.categories) # Global number of unique batches\n\n    # Train MMD-VAE\n    print(\"Initiating\
    \ MMD-VAE training...\")\n    X_emb_vae, _, vae_losses, recon_losses, kl_losses, mmd_losses = train_mmd_vae(\n        rng_key, X_hvg_dense, batch_labels_int, n_batches_global, # Pass global batch count\n        latent_dim=latent_dim, encoder_hidden_dims=encoder_hidden_dims,\n        decoder_hidden_dims=decoder_hidden_dims,\n        lr_vae=lr_vae, kl_weight=kl_weight, recon_weight=recon_weight, mmd_weight=mmd_weight,\n        epochs=epochs, batch_size=batch_size, mmd_sigma=mmd_sigma\n    )\n    print(\"✓ MMD-VAE training complete.\")\n    print(f\"MMD-VAE Embedding shape: {X_emb_vae.shape}\")\n\n    # Convert X_emb_vae to numpy for downstream sklearn/scipy functions\n    X_emb_vae_np = np.asarray(X_emb_vae)\n\n    # Construct graph from VAE latent space using Calibrated Balanced kNN\n    print(\"Constructing graph from VAE latent space...\")\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn_calibrated(\n        X_emb_vae_np, batch_labels_categorical.values, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib,\
    \ clamp=clamp\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_vae_np}, # Use the VAE's latent space as the embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_mmd_vae_bugfix_v3',\n            'mmd_vae_params': {\n                'latent_dim': latent_dim,\n                'encoder_hidden_dims': encoder_hidden_dims,\n                'decoder_hidden_dims': decoder_hidden_dims,\n                'lr_vae': lr_vae,\n                'kl_weight': kl_weight,\n                'recon_weight': recon_weight,\n                'mmd_weight': mmd_weight,\n                'mmd_sigma': mmd_sigma,\n                'epochs': epochs,\n                'batch_size': batch_size,\n                'hvg_method': \"scanpy_seurat_v3_batch_aware\",\n                'graph_type':\
    \ 'Calibrated Balanced kNN (on VAE latent space)'\n            },\n            'training_logs': {\n                'vae_losses': [float(l) for l in vae_losses],\n                'recon_losses': [float(l) for l in recon_losses],\n                'kl_losses': [float(l) for l in kl_losses],\n                'mmd_losses': [float(l) for l in mmd_losses],\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Calibrated Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: MMD-VAE pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n\
    \  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: MMD-VAE - Initial Implementation for Stable Batch Correction (Bugfix v3)\nInitiating MMD-VAE training...\nEpoch 0/300: VAE Loss=2426.8918 (Recon=2353.3833, KL=60.7497, MMD=0.4253)\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI\
    \ | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 302 | 1 | MNN Correction on Gene Expression Space | Veritas I | 177 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 301 | 1 | Aether II Dual BRBG: Soft-Whitening Tau Tuning (tau=0.94) | Aether II | 177 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.904 |\n| 300 | 1 | Sophia II: MMD-VAE - Bugfix for JAX Concretization Error | Sophia II | 177 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 299 | 1 | PCA-Combat Embedding with BBKNN Graph | Veritas I | 176 | 0.6190 | 0.586 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.789 |\n| 298 | 1 | Aether II Dual BRBG: Soft-Whitening Tau Tuning (tau=0.96) | Aether II | 176 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.072 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.907 |\n| 297 | 1 | Novel Method: Hybrid RBNG (PCA + Ranks) v1 | Daedalus II | 176 | 0.5368 | 0.024 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.770 | 0.058 | 1.000 | 0.574 | 0.994\
    \ | 0.872 |\n| 296 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=51) | Praxis I | 176 | 0.7303 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.058 | 0.945 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.933 | 0.947 |\n| 295 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.55, k=48) | Praxis I | 176 | 0.7238 | 0.740 | 0.858 | 0.157 | 0.066 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.870 |\n| 294 | 1 | kNN Graph on PCA-Combat Embedding | Veritas I | 175 | 0.3160 | 0.586 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.875 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.024 | 0.000 |\n| 293 | 1 | Sophia II: MMD-VAE - Initial Implementation for Stable Batch Correction | Sophia II | 175 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
