parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 194\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 316,710 / 600,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: MMD-VAE Optimization - Stronger Local MMD & Corrected k_calib' (ID: 337) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7008215723773594\n**ASW_batch:** 0.645\n**ASW_label:** 0.199\n**ARI:** 0.706\n**NMI:** 0.653\n**Graph_conn:** 0.949\n**kBET:** 0.798\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.915\n**PCR:** 0.995\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.213\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.645  ASW_label: 0.199  ARI: 0.706  NMI: 0.653\n  Graph_conn: 0.949  kBET: 0.798  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI:\
    \ 0.915\n  PCR: 0.995  Cell_cycle: 0.213\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.824070  ASW_label: 0.526493  ARI: 0.706181  NMI: 0.653305\n  Graph_conn: 0.949792  kBET: 0.761142  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.975270\n  PCR: 0.994983  Cell_cycle: 0.190523\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 337\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX JIT compilation errors in the MMD-VAE batch alignment loss function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code contained Python control flow statements (`if` conditionals) and boolean array indexing inside a function that was being JIT-compiled by JAX. Specifically:\n\n1. **Line 175 (original)**: `if n_samples_by_batch[b_idx] > 1:` - Attempted to use a traced JAX array in a Python boolean context\n2. **Line 211 (v2)**: `z_batch_data = z[batch_mask]` - Attempted to use dynamic boolean indexing on a JAX array\n\nJAX's JIT compiler cannot handle:\n- Python `if` statements with conditions that depend on\
    \ traced array values\n- Boolean array indexing with non-concrete (traced) boolean arrays\n\nBoth of these operations require the values to be known at compile time, but in a JIT-compiled function, the values are symbolic/traced and won't be known until runtime.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\n- Attempted to replace Python `if` statements with JAX-compatible operations\n- **Result**: Still failed due to boolean indexing `z[batch_mask]`\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - SUCCESSFUL\nCompletely rewrote `batch_mean_alignment_loss()` to use only JAX-compatible vectorized operations:\n\n1. **Removed all boolean indexing**: Instead of filtering by batch using `z[batch_mask]`, used vectorized operations with one-hot encoding\n2. **Replaced conditional logic**: Used `jnp.where()` and masking to handle conditional cases without Python `if` statements\n3. **Simplified algorithm**: Computed batch means using `einsum` for vectorized per-batch summation, then computed L2\
    \ distances to global mean\n4. **Added safety masks**: Multiplied distances by `batch_present_mask` to zero out contributions from empty batches\n\nKey changes in `batch_mean_alignment_loss()`:\n```python\n# Vectorized batch mean computation using einsum\none_hot_batch_labels = jax.nn.one_hot(batch_labels_batch, num_classes=n_batches_global)\nsum_z_by_batch = jnp.einsum('ij,ik->kj', z, one_hot_batch_labels)\nn_samples_by_batch = jnp.sum(one_hot_batch_labels, axis=0)\nbatch_means = sum_z_by_batch / jnp.maximum(n_samples_by_batch[:, None], 1.0)\n\n# Compute squared L2 distances (all batches at once)\ndistances_sq = jnp.sum(jnp.square(batch_means - z_global_mean[None, :]), axis=1)\n\n# Mask out empty batches\nbatch_present_mask = (n_samples_by_batch > 0).astype(jnp.float32)\ntotal_loss = jnp.sum(distances_sq * batch_present_mask)\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix maintains the mathematical intent of the original algorithm (aligning batch means to the global mean) while making it compatible\
    \ with JAX's JIT compilation constraints. The vectorized implementation:\n\n- Uses only operations that work with traced arrays\n- Computes results for all batches simultaneously (more efficient)\n- Handles edge cases (empty batches) through masking rather than conditionals\n- Fully compatible with automatic differentiation\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v3.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the JAX JIT compatibility issues have been resolved.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'  # Force JAX to use CPU only\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\nos.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\nimport jax\n# JIT is now ENABLED.\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport\
    \ anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD # Added for intermediate PCA\n\n# JAX and Flax imports\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax import linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax  # For optimizers\n\n# --- Helper functions (retained from Sophia I's SOTA / standard preprocessing) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    \"\"\"Compute HVGs using scanpy's batch-aware method (Seurat v3 flavor).\"\"\"\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        print(f\"Warning: Only {mask.sum()} HVGs found. Using all genes as HVGs.\")\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\n# --- Helper functions for Calibrated Balanced kNN from Praxis I's cbknn.py ---\ndef _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"Estimate per-batch distance scales.\"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    per_batch_meds = {}\n    all_meds = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size < 3:\n            per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n            all_meds.append(1.0)\n            continue\n        k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds =\
    \ nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        d_no_self = []\n        for i in range(idx.size):\n            di = dists[i]\n            gi = inds[i]\n            mask = gi != i\n            di = di[mask]\n            if di.size == 0: continue\n            d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n        if len(d_no_self) == 0: med = 1.0\n        else: med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n        per_batch_meds[b] = med\n        all_meds.append(med if med > 0 else 1.0)\n    ref = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n    scales = {}\n    lo, hi = clamp\n    for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n        if med <= 0: s = 1.0\n        else: s = ref / med\n        s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n        scales[b] = s\n    return scales\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_calib=16, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    \"\"\"Balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas and per-batch distance calibration.\"\
    \"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0: return None, None\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n    scales = _batch_distance_scales(Z, batches, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        q = quotas[b]\n        if idx.size == 0 or q == 0: continue\n        k = min(q + 1, idx.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx[inds]\n        scale_b = float(scales.get(b, 1.0))\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i] * scale_b\n\
    \            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:q]\n            di = di[mask][:q]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev): pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n# --- Flax Modules for VAE ---\n\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            x = nn.Dense(dim)(x)\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \            x = nn.relu(x)\n        mu = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        log_var = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return mu, log_var\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            z = nn.Dense(dim)(z)\n            z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n            z = nn.relu(z)\n        x_recon = nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(z)\n        return x_recon\n\n# --- Training State for Flax ---\n\nclass VAEState(train_state.TrainState):\n    pass\n\n# --- MMD Loss implementation (Batch Mean Alignment) - JAX-Compatible Version ---\ndef batch_mean_alignment_loss(z, batch_labels_batch, n_batches_global, mmd_sigma=1.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Batch mean alignment loss using JAX-compatible operations.\n    Computes squared L2 distance from each batch's mean to the global mean.\n    Uses vectorized operations compatible with JAX JIT.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Compute global mean\n    z_global_mean\
    \ = jnp.mean(z, axis=0)\n\n    # Create one-hot encoding for batch labels\n    one_hot_batch_labels = jax.nn.one_hot(batch_labels_batch, num_classes=n_batches_global)\n\n    # Compute per-batch sums using einsum (vectorized)\n    sum_z_by_batch = jnp.einsum('ij,ik->kj', z, one_hot_batch_labels)\n\n    # Count samples per batch\n    n_samples_by_batch = jnp.sum(one_hot_batch_labels, axis=0)\n\n    # Compute batch means (avoid division by zero)\n    batch_means = sum_z_by_batch / jnp.maximum(n_samples_by_batch[:, None], 1.0)\n\n    # Compute squared L2 distance from each batch mean to global mean\n    distances_sq = jnp.sum(jnp.square(batch_means - z_global_mean[None, :]), axis=1)\n\n    # Mask out batches with no samples (multiply by 1.0 if samples > 0, else 0.0)\n    batch_present_mask = (n_samples_by_batch > 0).astype(jnp.float32)\n\n    # Sum up distances, weighted by presence\n    total_loss = jnp.sum(distances_sq * batch_present_mask)\n\n    return total_loss\n\n# --- MMD-VAE Training\
    \ Loop ---\n\ndef train_mmd_vae(rng_key, X_input_to_vae, batch_labels_int, n_batches_global,\n                  latent_dim=128, encoder_hidden_dims=[256, 128],\n                  decoder_hidden_dims=[128, 256],\n                  lr_vae=1e-4, kl_weight=1.0, recon_weight=1.0, mmd_weight=10.0,\n                  epochs=100, batch_size=256, mmd_sigma=1.0):\n\n    n_cells, input_dim = X_input_to_vae.shape\n\n    rng_key, vae_key = jax.random.split(rng_key, 2)\n    encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=encoder_hidden_dims)\n    decoder = Decoder(output_dim=input_dim, hidden_dims=decoder_hidden_dims)\n\n    vae_params = {\n        'encoder': encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.zeros((1, input_dim)))['params'],\n        'decoder': decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.zeros((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    }\n    vae_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_vae)\n    vae_state = VAEState.create(apply_fn=lambda p, x: (encoder.apply({'params': p['encoder']}, x), decoder.apply({'params': p['decoder']}, x[0])),\n  \
    \                              params=vae_params,\n                                tx=vae_optimizer)\n\n    def mmd_vae_loss_fn(vae_params, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch):\n        mu, log_var = encoder.apply({'params': vae_params['encoder']}, x_batch)\n        std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n        epsilon = jax.random.normal(rng_key_vae_sample, mu.shape)\n        z = mu + std * epsilon\n        x_recon = decoder.apply({'params': vae_params['decoder']}, z)\n\n        recon_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(x_batch - x_recon), axis=-1))\n        kl_loss = -0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mu) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1))\n        # Pass mmd_sigma to the loss function\n        mmd_batch_loss = batch_mean_alignment_loss(z, batch_labels_batch, n_batches_global, mmd_sigma=mmd_sigma)\n\n        total_vae_loss = recon_weight * recon_loss + kl_weight * kl_loss + mmd_weight * mmd_batch_loss\n        return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss)\n\
    \n    @jax.jit\n    def vae_step(vae_state, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch):\n        (loss, (recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(mmd_vae_loss_fn, argnums=0, has_aux=True)(\n            vae_state.params, x_batch, rng_key_vae_sample, batch_labels_batch\n        )\n        vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n        return vae_state, loss, recon_loss, kl_loss, mmd_batch_loss\n\n    all_vae_losses, all_recon_losses, all_kl_losses, all_mmd_losses = [], [], [], []\n    unique_batches_global, batch_labels_mapped_global = np.unique(batch_labels_int, return_inverse=True)\n    batch_labels_mapped = jnp.array(batch_labels_mapped_global)\n    X_input_to_vae_jax = jnp.array(X_input_to_vae, dtype=jnp.float32)\n\n    for epoch in range(epochs):\n        rng_key, batch_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        permutation = jax.random.permutation(batch_key, n_cells)\n        shuffled_X = X_input_to_vae_jax[permutation]\n        shuffled_batch_labels\
    \ = batch_labels_mapped[permutation]\n\n        epoch_vae_loss, epoch_recon_loss, epoch_kl_loss, epoch_mmd_loss = 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0\n        num_batches_processed = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, n_cells, batch_size):\n            x_batch = shuffled_X[i:i + batch_size]\n            batch_labels_batch = shuffled_batch_labels[i:i + batch_size]\n            if x_batch.shape[0] == 0: continue\n            num_batches_processed += 1\n            rng_key, vae_sample_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n            vae_state, v_loss, r_loss, k_loss, mmd_loss = vae_step(vae_state, x_batch, vae_sample_key, batch_labels_batch)\n            epoch_vae_loss += v_loss; epoch_recon_loss += r_loss; epoch_kl_loss += k_loss; epoch_mmd_loss += mmd_loss\n\n        if num_batches_processed > 0:\n            epoch_vae_loss /= num_batches_processed; epoch_recon_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_kl_loss /= num_batches_processed; epoch_mmd_loss /= num_batches_processed\n\n        all_vae_losses.append(epoch_vae_loss);\
    \ all_recon_losses.append(epoch_recon_loss)\n        all_kl_losses.append(epoch_kl_loss); all_mmd_losses.append(epoch_mmd_loss)\n\n        if epoch % 10 == 0:\n            print(f\"Epoch {epoch}/{epochs}: VAE Loss={epoch_vae_loss:.4f} (Recon={epoch_recon_loss:.4f}, KL={epoch_kl_loss:.4f}, MMD={epoch_mmd_loss:.4f})\")\n\n    final_mu, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.params['encoder']}, X_input_to_vae_jax)\n    return final_mu, vae_state.params, all_vae_losses, all_recon_losses, all_kl_losses, all_mmd_losses\n\n\n# --- Soft-whitening function ---\ndef _soft_whiten_pcs(Z: jnp.ndarray, variance: np.ndarray, alpha=0.7, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Soft whitening: Z_scaled = Z / var^(alpha/2), where alpha in [0,1].\n    alpha=0 -> no change; alpha=1 -> full whitening. Recenter columns to 0 mean.\n    \"\"\"\n    if variance is None: return Z\n    var_jnp = jnp.array(variance[:Z.shape[1]])\n    scale = jnp.power(jnp.clip(var_jnp, eps, None), 0.5 * float(alpha))\n    scale = jnp.where(scale\
    \ > 0, scale, 1.0) # Avoid division by zero\n\n    Zw = Z / scale\n    Zw -= jnp.mean(Zw, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Zw\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: MMD-VAE Optimization - Stronger Local MMD & Corrected k_calib\")\n\n    # VAE Configuration\n    latent_dim = 128\n    encoder_hidden_dims = [256, 128]\n    decoder_hidden_dims = [128, 256]\n\n    lr_vae = 1e-4\n    kl_weight = 2.0 # Increased KL weight\n    recon_weight = 1.0\n    mmd_weight = 50.0 # Increased MMD loss weight\n    mmd_sigma = 0.8 # Tuned Gaussian kernel bandwidth for more local alignment\n    epochs = 100\n    batch_size = 256\n\n    # Intermediate PCA and Soft-Whitening parameters\n    n_intermediate_pcs = 50 # Dimension for PCA before VAE\n    alpha_soft_whiten = 0.7 # From Praxis I's example\n\n    # Graph construction parameters (from Sophia I's SOTA)\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    k_calib\
    \ = 24 # Corrected from 16 to 24 (typo fix)\n    clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n\n    random_state = 0\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Preprocessing\n    adata_processed = adata.copy()\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_processed, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_processed, n_top_genes=2000)\n\n    X_hvg_dense_np = adata_processed.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if sp.issparse(X_hvg_dense_np):\n        X_hvg_dense_np = X_hvg_dense_np.toarray()\n\n    # Intermediate PCA\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_intermediate_pcs, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z_hvg_pca_np = svd.fit_transform(X_hvg_dense_np)\n    pca_variance_np = svd.explained_variance_\n\n    # Apply Soft-Whitening\n    Z_input_to_vae_jax = _soft_whiten_pcs(jnp.array(Z_hvg_pca_np, dtype=jnp.float32), pca_variance_np, alpha=alpha_soft_whiten)\n\
    \n    batch_labels_categorical = adata_processed.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels_int = batch_labels_categorical.cat.codes.values\n    n_batches_global = len(batch_labels_categorical.cat.categories)\n\n    # Train MMD-VAE\n    print(\"Initiating MMD-VAE training with Soft-Whitened PCA input...\")\n    X_emb_vae, _, vae_losses, recon_losses, kl_losses, mmd_losses = train_mmd_vae(\n        rng_key, Z_input_to_vae_jax, batch_labels_int, n_batches_global,\n        latent_dim=latent_dim, encoder_hidden_dims=encoder_hidden_dims,\n        decoder_hidden_dims=decoder_hidden_dims,\n        lr_vae=lr_vae, kl_weight=kl_weight, recon_weight=recon_weight, mmd_weight=mmd_weight,\n        epochs=epochs, batch_size=batch_size, mmd_sigma=mmd_sigma\n    )\n    print(\"✓ MMD-VAE training complete.\")\n    print(f\"MMD-VAE Embedding shape: {X_emb_vae.shape}\")\n\n    X_emb_vae_np = np.asarray(X_emb_vae)\n\n    # Construct graph from VAE latent space using Calibrated Balanced kNN\n    print(\"\
    Constructing graph from VAE latent space...\")\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn_calibrated(\n        X_emb_vae_np, batch_labels_categorical.values, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_emb_vae_np},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_mmd_vae_softwhiten_pca_input_mmd50_kl2_kcalib24_fixed',\n            'mmd_vae_params': {\n                'latent_dim': latent_dim,\n                'encoder_hidden_dims': encoder_hidden_dims,\n                'decoder_hidden_dims': decoder_hidden_dims,\n                'lr_vae': lr_vae,\n                'kl_weight': kl_weight,\n                'recon_weight': recon_weight,\n                'mmd_weight': mmd_weight,\n                'mmd_sigma':\
    \ mmd_sigma,\n                'mmd_loss_type': 'Batch Mean Alignment (L2, Vectorized, JAX-Compatible)',\n                'epochs': epochs,\n                'batch_size': batch_size,\n                'hvg_method': \"scanpy_seurat_v3_batch_aware\",\n                'intermediate_pca_dims': n_intermediate_pcs,\n                'soft_whiten_alpha': alpha_soft_whiten,\n                'graph_type': 'Calibrated Balanced kNN (on VAE latent space)'\n            },\n            'training_logs': {\n                'vae_losses': [float(l) for l in vae_losses],\n                'recon_losses': [float(l) for l in recon_losses],\n                'kl_losses': [float(l) for l in kl_losses],\n                'mmd_losses': [float(l) for l in mmd_losses],\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\
    \ 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Calibrated Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: MMD-VAE pipeline complete with Soft-Whitened PCA input.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: MMD-VAE Optimization - Stronger Local MMD & Corrected k_calib\nInitiating MMD-VAE training with Soft-Whitened PCA input...\nEpoch 0/100: VAE Loss=1443.6594 (Recon=98.7159, KL=43.3269, MMD=25.1658)\nEpoch 10/100: VAE Loss=402.1756 (Recon=75.0474, KL=57.7476, MMD=4.2327)\nEpoch 20/100: VAE Loss=349.4789 (Recon=70.1371, KL=70.1642, MMD=2.7803)\nEpoch 30/100: VAE Loss=325.5121 (Recon=68.9862, KL=64.7736, MMD=2.5396)\nEpoch 40/100:\
    \ VAE Loss=285.6712 (Recon=68.2985, KL=55.3794, MMD=2.1323)\nEpoch 50/100: VAE Loss=259.3498 (Recon=67.1390, KL=47.7387, MMD=1.9347)\nEpoch 60/100: VAE Loss=247.8647 (Recon=65.4201, KL=46.2284, MMD=1.7998)\nEpoch 70/100: VAE Loss=253.1114 (Recon=64.0475, KL=45.3376, MMD=1.9678)\nEpoch 80/100: VAE Loss=240.5277 (Recon=62.8037, KL=44.5963, MMD=1.7706)\nEpoch 90/100: VAE Loss=239.5020 (Recon=61.5651, KL=45.5995, MMD=1.7348)\n✓ MMD-VAE training complete.\nMMD-VAE Embedding shape: (20000, 128)\nConstructing graph from VAE latent space...\n✓ Graph path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: MMD-VAE pipeline complete with Soft-Whitened PCA input.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8d0189de-4ee3-4b51-b8f8-276ac2191788/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8d0189de-4ee3-4b51-b8f8-276ac2191788\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last\
