    For clarity and direct comparison, I will aim to make the non-LCCM parts of the alternative baseline experiment match Veritas I''s "Combat Manual Baseline" as closely as possible. This means explicitly including a `sc.pp.combat` call, if `Combat Manual` uses it, rather than my `get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes`, to truly reflect a different baseline. I will verify `Combat Manual`''s code (if available to read) or emulate it closely.


    **Data Consistency for Generalization (Experiment 5):**


    For Experiment 5 (LCCM with Different Latent Dimension), `n_pcs_emb` will be increased from 64 to 100 or 128. This directly tests the robustness of LCCM to the richness of the input embedding. It implies that the `lccm_output_dim` will automatically adjust. This is a sound test of generalizability within the same dataset and primary baseline.


    **Final Check on Reviewer Feedback:**


    *   **"Completely abandon this format":** My new approach, with a structured paper (Introduction, Methods, Results, Conclusion), addresses this.

    *   **"Select your most promising idea":** LCCM is chosen.

