parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 223\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 459,516 / 600,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 99 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05)' (ID: 397) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.45341858592966167\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.167\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.052\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.167  iLISI: 0.935 \
    \ cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.052\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.017486  ASW_label: 0.204801  ARI: 0.736436  NMI: 0.700563\n  Graph_conn: 0.972128  kBET: 0.167861  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991751\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.053700\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 397\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import statements. Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 0.453.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code used `warnings.catch_warnings()` and `ConvergenceWarning` in the `get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes()` function but failed to import these modules at the top of the file.\n\nSpecifically:\n- Line 96 of the original code used `with warnings.catch_warnings():` without importing `warnings`\n- Line 96 also referenced `ConvergenceWarning` without importing it from `sklearn.exceptions`\n\nThis resulted in a `NameError: name 'warnings' is not defined` when the code attempted to execute.\n\n##\
    \ Fix Applied\nAdded two missing import statements at the top of submission_v2.py:\n\n```python\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n```\n\nThese imports enable the code to:\n1. Use `warnings.catch_warnings()` context manager to suppress convergence warnings during the iterative ComBat algorithm\n2. Specifically filter `ConvergenceWarning` exceptions from scikit-learn\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Running successfully\n- **Score**: 0.453\n- **Fix Type**: Simple import addition - no algorithmic changes required\n\nThe batch integration algorithm (Sophia II's Soft Quota kNN approach) now executes correctly with the complete import set.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse\
    \ as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# --- Helper functions from Sophia I's SOTA (ID 201) baseline ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1]\
    \ > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0):\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n    sse = np.sum((y - yhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n    y_center = y - np.mean(y, axis=0,\
    \ keepdims=True)\n    sst = np.sum(y_center ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n    r2 = 1.0 - (sse / sst)\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2, gamma_j\n\n# --- Praxis I's build_balanced_knn_soft for MSANF/Soft Quota (from Private Memory Capsule 32) ---\n# Pasted here for direct integration\ndef build_balanced_knn_soft(Z, batches, k_total=48, tau=0.05, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Soft-quota balanced kNN with a single temperature τ:\n      - Base equal quotas across batches (floor(k/nb)).\n      - Distribute the remainder to batches with higher local affinity scores\n        (sum of exp(-d/τ) over candidate neighbors), τ>0.\n      - Within each batch, pick nearest neighbors up to its quota.\n      - Symmetric union; binary connectivities; distances = min distance on duplicate edges.\n    τ→0 approximates equal-quotas (deterministic); larger τ emphasizes closer batches for remainders.\n\
    \    Returns: (C, D) CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0 or k_total <= 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n\n    k_per_batch = base + (rem if rem > 0 else 0) + 1\n    per_batch_inds = {}\n    per_batch_dists = {}\n    per_batch_scores = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0:\n            continue\n        kq = min(k_per_batch, idx_b.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        d, ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=kq, return_distance=True)\n        ind_global = idx_b[ind_local]\n        mask = ind_global != np.arange(n)[:, None]\n        ig = []\n        dg = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            m = mask[i]\n            g = ind_global[i][m]\n\
    \            di = d[i][m]\n            ig.append(g)\n            dg.append(di)\n        per_batch_inds[b] = ig\n        per_batch_dists[b] = dg\n        if tau > 0:\n            scores = [np.sum(np.exp(-di / tau)[:base + rem]) if di.size else 0.0 for di in dg]\n        else:\n            scores = [float(base + rem) for _ in range(n)]\n        per_batch_scores[b] = np.asarray(scores, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    quotas = {b: np.full(n, base, dtype=np.int32) for b in uniq}\n    if rem > 0:\n        for i in range(n):\n            bs = []\n            for b in uniq:\n                if b in per_batch_scores:\n                    bs.append((per_batch_scores[b][i], b))\n            if not bs:\n                continue\n            bs.sort(reverse=True)\n            for _, b in bs[:rem]:\n                quotas[b][i] += 1\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        if b not in per_batch_inds:\n            continue\n        for i in range(n):\n            q = int(quotas[b][i])\n   \
    \         if q <= 0:\n                continue\n            g = per_batch_inds[b][i]\n            di = per_batch_dists[b][i]\n            if g is None or len(g) == 0:\n                continue\n            g = g[:q]\n            di = di[:q]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    l2 = 1e-3\n\n    BtB = batch_design.T @ batch_design\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), batch_design.T @ data.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (batch_design @ W).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (batch_design.T @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:,\
    \ batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n            n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n            while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n                g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:,\
    \ np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n                d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n            gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05)\")\n\n    # SOTA Config parameters (Sophia I's ID 201 baseline)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.75\n    lam_adapt = 1.0\n    l2 = 1e-3\n\
    \    k_total = 48 # This k_total is for Soft Quota kNN\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    # k_calib is not used by build_balanced_knn_soft\n    clamp = (0.5, 2.0) # Used by Soft Quota's internal _batch_distance_scales if I were to re-implement, but build_balanced_knn_soft does not expose clamp\n    tau_soft_quota = 0.05 # Soft Quota specific parameter\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Create fresh copies of original adata (raw counts) for independent processing paths\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: Robust ComBat -> PCA (Baseline, untouched) ---\n    X_combat_corrected_full_genes = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_for_embedding_path)\n\n    adata_emb_processed_for_pca = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_combat_corrected_full_genes,\n      \
    \  obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    adata_emb_processed_for_pca.var_names = adata_for_embedding_path.var_names.copy()\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path, n_top_genes=2000)\n    adata_emb_processed_for_pca.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb_processed_for_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb = np.asarray(adata_emb_processed_for_pca.obsm['X_pca'])\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path: Adaptive Residualization -> Soft Quota kNN (Modification for Exp 2.1) ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path, n_top_genes=2000)\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_graph\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph):\n        X_graph =\
    \ sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt\n    )\n\n    # Build graph using Soft Quota kNN\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn_soft(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, tau=tau_soft_quota, metric=metric\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ Soft Quota kNN graph path complete. Graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_softquota_knn_exp2.1_tau005',\n            'baseline_parameters_embedding': {\n                'embedding_baseline': 'Robust ComBat\
    \ PCA on HVGs',\n                'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n            },\n            'graph_parameters_softquota': {\n                'gamma_max_adaptive': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'lam_adaptive': float(lam_adapt),\n                'l2': float(l2),\n                'k_total': int(k_total),\n                'metric': metric,\n                'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                'tau_soft_quota': float(tau_soft_quota),\n                'graph_source': 'Adaptively Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n                'graph_type': 'Soft Quota Balanced kNN'\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Soft Quota Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n\
    \    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: Soft Quota kNN-enhanced Dual BRBG pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05)\n✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: (20000, 64)\n✓ Soft Quota kNN graph path complete. Graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: Soft Quota kNN-enhanced Dual BRBG pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/380668c2-4145-4343-88de-40c67bcd2501/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 380668c2-4145-4343-88de-40c67bcd2501\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 400 | 1 | Analysis: Biological Signal Preservation in PC vs Gene Space | Daedalus II | 223 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 399 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (gamma_max=0.75) | Praxis I | 223 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 398 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors\
    \ (v2) | Daedalus II | 222 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 397 | 1 | Sophia II: Stagnation Exp 2.1 - Soft Quota kNN in Graph Path (τ=0.05) | Sophia II | 221 | 0.4534 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.052 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 0.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.167 |\n| 396 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Soft-Whiten Embedding (tau=0.95): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Whitening | Praxis I | 221 | 0.7148 | 0.744 | 0.837 | 0.168 | 0.107 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.742 |\n| 395 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA64 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 221 | 0.7320 | 0.744 | 0.690 | 0.216 | 0.351 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.768 |\n| 394 | 1 | Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors | Daedalus II | 220 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 393 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=45) | Praxis I | 220 | 0.7327 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 392 | 1 | SOTA Replication:\
    \ Daedalus II's EtC + Praxis I's BRBG | Veritas I | 219 | 0.6239 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.780 |\n| 391 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 219 | 0.7328 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for\
    \ the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
