- text: "My experimental plan for LCCM is finalized, covering baseline replication, refinement, and generalization tests. This tick focuses on double-checking the code structure and ensuring all helper functions are correctly defined and used. I must also re-verify the Python `warnings` and `sklearn.exceptions.ConvergenceWarning` imports.\n\n**Code Structure and Helper Functions Check:**\n\n1.  **`_normalize_log1p_inplace`:** Confirmed. Standard scanpy operation, correctly applied to adata.\n2.  **`_get_hvg_mask`:** Confirmed. Standard scanpy HVG selection, correctly applied.\n3.  **`_pca_truncated_svd`:** This helper was used in Sophia I's SOTA but is **not needed** for the new simple baseline, which directly uses `sc.pp.pca`. I will remove this helper to streamline the code and avoid confusion.\n4.  **`_one_hot_batches`, `_ridge_batch_fit_predict`, `adaptive_residualize`:** These helpers were part of Sophia I's Adaptive Residualization graph path. The new simple baseline uses `sc.pp.neighbors`\
    \ for graph construction, which **does not require** these functions. I will remove them to keep the code clean and token-efficient.\n5.  **`_batch_distance_scales`, `build_balanced_knn_calibrated`:** These were also part of Sophia I's complex graph construction. The new simple baseline's graph construction uses `sc.pp.neighbors`, which **does not require** these functions. I will remove them.\n6.  **`get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes`:** This was my custom robust Combat. The new simple baseline uses `sc.pp.combat` directly. I will **remove this helper function** and directly use `sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')`.\n7.  **`Decorrelator` and `DecorrelatorState`:** Confirmed. These are my custom Flax modules for LCCM, correctly defined.\n8.  **`lccm_loss_fn`, `lccm_step`:** Confirmed. These are the JAX-compatible loss and update functions for LCCM training. The vectorized cross-covariance calculation is in place.\n9.  **Imports:** I must ensure that `import warnings` and `from\
    \ sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning` are at the top of the script, as previously identified by the debugger.\n\n**Consolidated and Streamlined `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` Outline (General for all LCCM experiments):**\n\n```python\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n# Other necessary imports (numpy, scanpy, anndata, scipy.sparse, etc.)\n# JAX/Flax imports\n\n# Define _normalize_log1p_inplace and _get_hvg_mask (simple helpers)\n\n# Define Decorrelator and DecorrelatorState (my LCCM module)\n\n# Define lccm_loss_fn and lccm_step (JAX-compiled LCCM training steps)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration (Baseline & LCCM parameters) ---\n    N_PCS_EMB = ...\n    N_NEIGHBORS = ...\n    # LCCM params: alpha_decorrelation, beta_reconstruction, etc.\n    random_state = 0\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n    # --- Preprocessing ---\n    adata_pipeline = adata.copy()\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_pipeline)\n\
    \    _get_hvg_mask(adata_pipeline) # HVG mask created\n    \n    # --- Baseline Embedding Pathway (Combat -> PCA) ---\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_pipeline, key='batch') # Standard scanpy Combat\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_pipeline, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_emb_pca_np = adata_pipeline.obsm['X_pca'] # This is the input to LCCM\n\n    # --- LCCM Training (if applicable) ---\n    if LCCM_IS_ACTIVE: # Placeholder for conditional execution in baseline vs LCCM experiments\n        # Initialize and train Decorrelator\n        # X_emb_refined_jax = lccm_encoder.apply(final_lccm_params, X_emb_pca_jax)\n        Z_emb = np.asarray(X_emb_refined_jax) # Use refined embedding\n    else:\n        Z_emb = X_emb_pca_np # Use original PCA embedding for baseline\n\n    # --- Graph Construction (Simple kNN on final embedding) ---\n    # Ensure adata_pipeline has the final embedding in .obsm['X_emb'] for sc.pp.neighbors\n    adata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = Z_emb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=N_NEIGHBORS, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(...)\n    adata_out.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_emb\n    adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_pipeline.obsp['connectivities']\n    adata_out.obsp['distances'] = adata_pipeline.obsp['distances']\n    adata_out.uns['method_id'] = ... # Document method and parameters\n\n    return adata_out\n```\n\nThis streamlined code template will ensure consistency across all LCCM experiments and minimize token usage, adhering to all reviewer feedback and stagnation protocol guidelines. This final check increases my confidence in the upcoming experimental phase. I am ready."
