tick: 226
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sophia II, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. The station is in stagnation, and my token usage is at 79%. I am about to submit code for **Experiment A (New Baseline Replication)**. This is a critical first step to establish a stable and reproducible baseline (Veritas I's \"PCA-based Combat Correction,\" ID 292) before integrating LCCM. I will use a simple `sc.pp.combat` followed by `sc.pp.pca` for embedding, and `sc.pp.neighbors` for graph construction, reflecting a simple and modular baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia II: LCCM Experiment A - Baseline Replication (Veritas I: PCA-based Combat Correction)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, baseline, replication, combat, pca, knn, simple\"\nabstract: \"Replication of Veritas I's 'PCA-based Combat Correction' (ID 292) to establish a simple, robust, and reproducible baseline. This pipeline uses standard Scanpy preprocessing, `sc.pp.combat` for batch correction, `sc.pp.pca` for embedding, and\
    \ `sc.pp.neighbors` for graph construction. This serves as the foundation for subsequent LCCM experiments under the Stagnation Protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import warnings\n  from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n  # --- Helper functions (minimal for simple baseline) ---\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n      if mask.sum() < 10:\n    \
    \      return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n      return mask\n\n  # --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for simple baseline ---\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Sophia II: LCCM Experiment A - Baseline Replication (Veritas I: PCA-based Combat Correction)\")\n\n      # Baseline Configuration (reflecting Veritas I ID 292 and common practice)\n      N_PCS_EMB = 50\n      N_NEIGHBORS = 15 # Standard for simple kNN graph\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n      adata_pipeline = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- Preprocessing ---\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_pipeline)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_pipeline)\n      adata_pipeline.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask # Ensure HVG mask is set\n\n      # --- Embedding Pathway (Combat -> PCA) ---\n      # Suppress ConvergenceWarning\
    \ from sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression within sc.pp.combat if it uses it internally\n      with warnings.catch_warnings():\n          warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n          sc.pp.combat(adata_pipeline, key='batch') # Standard scanpy Combat\n\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_pipeline, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z_emb = np.asarray(adata_pipeline.obsm['X_pca'])\n      print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete (Combat+PCA). Embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n      # --- Graph Construction (Simple kNN on final embedding) ---\n      adata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_emb # Set the embedding for neighbors calculation\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=N_NEIGHBORS, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n      \n      C = adata_pipeline.obsp['connectivities']\n      D = adata_pipeline.obsp['distances']\n      print(f\"✓ Graph path complete (Simple kNN). Graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else\
    \ 'Failed'}\")\n\n      # --- Final Output Construction ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, # Use the Combat+PCA embedding\n          uns={\n              'method_id': 'sophia_II_lccm_expA_baseline_replication',\n              'baseline_parameters': {\n                  'normalization': 'normalize_total+log1p',\n                  'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                  'batch_correction_method': 'scanpy.pp.combat',\n                  'embedding_method': 'PCA',\n                  'pcs_emb': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                  'graph_method': 'scanpy.pp.neighbors',\n                  'n_neighbors_graph': int(N_NEIGHBORS),\n                  'metric': 'cosine'\n              }\n          }\n      )\n\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors']\
    \ = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      else:\n          print(\"Warning: Simple kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n      print(f\"✓ Sophia II: Simple Baseline pipeline complete.\")\n      return adata_out\n```"
