tick: 230
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 230\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 488,739 / 600,000 used (81%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: LCCM Experiment B - Moderated Decorrelation on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0)' (ID: 410) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6158989175026685\n**ASW_batch:** 0.596\n**ASW_label:** 0.236\n**ARI:** 0.638\n**NMI:** 0.715\n**Graph_conn:** 0.896\n**kBET:** 0.660\n**iLISI:** 0.068\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.358\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.596  ASW_label: 0.236  ARI: 0.638  NMI: 0.715\n  Graph_conn: 0.896  kBET: 0.660\
    \  iLISI: 0.068  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.358\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.801995  ASW_label: 0.547869  ARI: 0.638089  NMI: 0.714872\n  Graph_conn: 0.898230  kBET: 0.631900  iLISI: 0.068065  cLISI: 0.997407\n  PCR: 0.999757  Cell_cycle: 0.314528\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 410\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Numba typing error in neighbor computation. Code now runs successfully and achieved a score of **0.6159**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with a **Numba TypingError** during the `sc.pp.neighbors()` call using the cosine metric. The error occurred because:\n\n1. JAX arrays converted to numpy arrays via `np.asarray()` can be **read-only**\n2. The pynndescent library (used by scanpy for neighbor computation) uses Numba JIT compilation\n3. Numba's typed arrays require writable arrays, but the read-only flag caused a signature mismatch:\n   - Expected: `Array(float32, 2, 'C', False, aligned=True)` (writable)\n\
    \   - Got: `readonly array(float32, 2d, C)` (read-only)\n\nThis manifested as:\n```\nInvalid use of type(CPUDispatcher(<function angular_random_projection_split>))\nKnown signatures: (Array(float32, 2, 'C', False, aligned=True), ...)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nApplied two defensive fixes to ensure array compatibility:\n\n### Fix 1: JAX to NumPy Conversion (Line 116)\n**Before:**\n```python\nreturn np.asarray(X_emb_refined_jax)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nreturn np.array(X_emb_refined_jax, copy=True)\n```\n\n**Rationale:** Using `np.array(..., copy=True)` guarantees a writable copy, unlike `np.asarray()` which may return a read-only view.\n\n### Fix 2: Ensure C-Contiguous Array (Line 196)\n**Before:**\n```python\nZ_emb = Z_emb_lccm_refined\nadata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_emb\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=N_NEIGHBORS, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nZ_emb = Z_emb_lccm_refined\nZ_emb = np.ascontiguousarray(Z_emb)\nadata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = Z_emb\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=N_NEIGHBORS, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n```\n\n**Rationale:** `np.ascontiguousarray()` ensures the array is C-contiguous and writable, which is optimal for Numba-compiled functions.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type:** Runtime error during Numba JIT compilation\n- **Failure Point:** `sc.pp.neighbors()` → `pynndescent` → `make_angular_tree()` → `angular_random_projection_split()`\n- **Environment:** Python 3.11, batch_integration conda environment\n- **Score Achieved:** 0.6159\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using `monitor_evaluation.py 2`, which confirmed:\n- Code executed without crashing\n- Evaluation completed successfully\n- Score was properly computed and saved\n\n## Files Modified\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py` - Complete fixed implementation\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'  # Force JAX to use CPU only\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=1'\nos.environ['JAX_ENABLE_X64'] = 'False'\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax import linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# --- Helper functions (minimal for simple baseline) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\n# --- LCCM Module ---\n\nclass Decorrelator(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int # Should match input_dim (PCA latent_dim)\n    hidden_dims: list\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            x = nn.Dense(dim)(x)\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n        # Final layer outputs the refined embedding\n        refined_embedding = nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(x)\n        return refined_embedding\n\nclass DecorrelatorState(train_state.TrainState):\n    pass\n\n# --- LCCM Training Loop (JAX-compiled) ---\n\n# Meticulously verified JAX-compatible cross-covariance calculation.\ndef _calculate_cross_covariance(X_emb_refined, one_hot_batch_labels, n_batches_global):\n    centered_X_emb = X_emb_refined -\
    \ jnp.mean(X_emb_refined, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    centered_B = one_hot_batch_labels - jnp.mean(one_hot_batch_labels, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    cross_cov = jnp.einsum('ni,nj->ij', centered_X_emb, centered_B) / (X_emb_refined.shape[0] - 1)\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.square(cross_cov))\n\ndef train_lccm_decorrelator(rng_key, X_emb_pca_jax, batch_labels_mapped, n_batches_global,\n                            lccm_input_dim, lccm_output_dim, lccm_hidden_dims,\n                            lr_lccm, alpha_decorrelation, beta_reconstruction,\n                            lccm_epochs, lccm_batch_size):\n\n    lccm_encoder = Decorrelator(output_dim=lccm_output_dim, hidden_dims=lccm_hidden_dims)\n    lccm_params = lccm_encoder.init(rng_key, jnp.zeros((1, lccm_input_dim)))['params']\n    lccm_optimizer = optax.adam(lr_lccm)\n    lccm_state = DecorrelatorState.create(apply_fn=lccm_encoder.apply,\n                                          params=lccm_params,\n                                    \
    \      tx=lccm_optimizer)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def lccm_loss_fn(lccm_params, x_batch_pca, batch_labels_batch):\n        X_emb_refined = lccm_encoder.apply({'params': lccm_params}, x_batch_pca)\n        decorrelation_loss = _calculate_cross_covariance(X_emb_refined, jax.nn.one_hot(batch_labels_batch, num_classes=n_batches_global), n_batches_global)\n        reconstruction_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jnp.square(X_emb_refined - x_batch_pca), axis=-1))\n        total_lccm_loss = alpha_decorrelation * decorrelation_loss + beta_reconstruction * reconstruction_loss\n        return total_lccm_loss, (decorrelation_loss, reconstruction_loss)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def lccm_step(lccm_state, x_batch_pca, batch_labels_batch):\n        (loss, (decorrelation_loss, reconstruction_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(lccm_loss_fn, has_aux=True)(\n            lccm_state.params, x_batch_pca, batch_labels_batch\n        )\n        lccm_state = lccm_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n        return lccm_state,\
    \ loss, decorrelation_loss, reconstruction_loss\n\n    n_cells_lccm = X_emb_pca_jax.shape[0]\n    for epoch in range(lccm_epochs):\n        rng_key, batch_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        permutation = jax.random.permutation(batch_key, n_cells_lccm)\n        shuffled_X_pca = X_emb_pca_jax[permutation]\n        shuffled_batch_labels = batch_labels_mapped[permutation]\n\n        epoch_lccm_loss, epoch_decorrelation_loss, epoch_reconstruction_loss = 0.0, 0.0, 0.0\n        num_batches_processed = 0\n\n        for i in range(0, n_cells_lccm, lccm_batch_size):\n            x_batch_pca = shuffled_X_pca[i:i + lccm_batch_size]\n            batch_labels_batch = shuffled_batch_labels[i:i + lccm_batch_size]\n            if x_batch_pca.shape[0] == 0: continue\n\n            num_batches_processed += 1\n            lccm_state, l_loss, d_loss, r_loss = lccm_step(lccm_state, x_batch_pca, batch_labels_batch)\n            epoch_lccm_loss += l_loss\n            epoch_decorrelation_loss += d_loss\n\
    \            epoch_reconstruction_loss += r_loss\n\n        if num_batches_processed > 0:\n            epoch_lccm_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_decorrelation_loss /= num_batches_processed\n            epoch_reconstruction_loss /= num_batches_processed\n\n        if epoch % 10 == 0:\n            print(f\"LCCM Epoch {epoch}/{lccm_epochs}: Total Loss={epoch_lccm_loss:.4f} (Decorrelation={epoch_decorrelation_loss:.4f}, Recon={epoch_reconstruction_loss:.4f})\")\n\n    X_emb_refined_jax = lccm_encoder.apply({'params': lccm_state.params}, X_emb_pca_jax)\n    # CRITICAL FIX: Ensure array is writable by making a copy\n    return np.array(X_emb_refined_jax, copy=True)\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: LCCM Experiment B - Moderated Decorrelation on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0)\")\n\n    # Baseline Configuration (reflecting Veritas I ID 292 and common practice)\n    N_PCS_EMB =\
    \ 50\n    N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n    random_state = 0\n    rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(random_state)\n\n    # LCCM Configuration (Experiment B changes: alpha_decorrelation from 10.0 to 5.0)\n    lccm_hidden_dims = [64, 32]\n    lr_lccm = 1e-3\n    alpha_decorrelation = 5.0\n    beta_reconstruction = 1.0\n    lccm_epochs = 50\n    lccm_batch_size = 256\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    adata_pipeline = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_pipeline)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_pipeline)\n    adata_pipeline.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask # Ensure HVG mask is set\n\n    # --- Embedding Pathway (Combat -> PCA) ---\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(adata_pipeline, key='batch')\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_pipeline, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB,\
    \ use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_emb_pca_np = adata_pipeline.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"✓ Baseline Embedding (Combat+PCA) shape: {X_emb_pca_np.shape}\")\n\n    # --- LCCM Training and Application ---\n    print(\"Initiating LCCM Decorrelator training...\")\n    lccm_input_dim = X_emb_pca_np.shape[1]\n    lccm_output_dim = lccm_input_dim\n\n    # Prepare data for LCCM training\n    X_emb_pca_jax = jnp.array(X_emb_pca_np, dtype=jnp.float32)\n    batch_labels_categorical = adata_pipeline.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels_int = batch_labels_categorical.cat.codes.values\n    n_batches_global = len(batch_labels_categorical.cat.categories)\n    batch_labels_mapped = jnp.array(batch_labels_int)\n\n    Z_emb_lccm_refined = train_lccm_decorrelator(\n        rng_key, X_emb_pca_jax, batch_labels_mapped, n_batches_global,\n        lccm_input_dim, lccm_output_dim, lccm_hidden_dims,\n        lr_lccm, alpha_decorrelation, beta_reconstruction,\n\
    \        lccm_epochs, lccm_batch_size\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ LCCM Embedding path complete. Refined embedding shape: {Z_emb_lccm_refined.shape}\")\n    Z_emb = Z_emb_lccm_refined # Use LCCM-refined embedding\n\n    # --- Graph Construction (Simple kNN on final embedding) ---\n    # ADDITIONAL FIX: Ensure the array is C-contiguous and writable\n    Z_emb = np.ascontiguousarray(Z_emb)\n    adata_pipeline.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_emb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pipeline, n_neighbors=N_NEIGHBORS, use_rep='X_emb', metric='cosine')\n\n    C = adata_pipeline.obsp['connectivities']\n    D = adata_pipeline.obsp['distances']\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete (Simple kNN). Graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_lccm_expB_alpha5_beta1',\n            'baseline_parameters': {\n\
    \                'normalization': 'normalize_total+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'batch_correction_method': 'scanpy.pp.combat',\n                'embedding_method': 'PCA',\n                'pcs_emb': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'graph_method': 'scanpy.pp.neighbors',\n                'n_neighbors_graph': int(N_NEIGHBORS),\n                'metric': 'cosine'\n            },\n            'lccm_parameters': {\n                'lccm_hidden_dims': lccm_hidden_dims,\n                'lr_lccm': lr_lccm,\n                'alpha_decorrelation': alpha_decorrelation,\n                'beta_reconstruction': beta_reconstruction,\n                'lccm_epochs': lccm_epochs,\n                'lccm_batch_size': lccm_batch_size,\n                'embedding_enhancement': 'Latent Correlation Minimization Post-PCA'\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n \
    \       adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Simple kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: LCCM-enhanced Simple Baseline pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: LCCM Experiment B - Moderated Decorrelation on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0)\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n✓ Baseline Embedding (Combat+PCA) shape: (20000, 50)\nInitiating LCCM Decorrelator training...\nLCCM Epoch 0/50: Total Loss=449.5781 (Decorrelation=0.0005, Recon=449.5756)\nLCCM Epoch 10/50: Total Loss=88.5676 (Decorrelation=0.0056,\
    \ Recon=88.5396)\nLCCM Epoch 20/50: Total Loss=62.6810 (Decorrelation=0.0058, Recon=62.6518)\nLCCM Epoch 30/50: Total Loss=57.7845 (Decorrelation=0.0054, Recon=57.7576)\nLCCM Epoch 40/50: Total Loss=55.3269 (Decorrelation=0.0064, Recon=55.2949)\n✓ LCCM Embedding path complete. Refined embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ Graph path complete (Simple kNN). Graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: LCCM-enhanced Simple Baseline pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/2d926721-63b5-49d7-9103-52f6a207a8cf/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 2d926721-63b5-49d7-9103-52f6a207a8cf\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 410 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment B - Moderated Decorrelation on Simple Baseline (alpha=5.0) | Sophia II | 228 | 0.6159\
    \ | 0.638 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.358 | 0.896 | 0.715 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.068 | 0.660 |\n| 409 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=51) | Praxis I | 228 | 0.7325 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.782 |\n| 408 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v3): EtC + Correct BRBG (Imported) | Veritas I | 227 | 0.6211 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.324 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.781 |\n| 407 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + PBVE-Emb (alpha=0.2): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Gentle Variance Equalization | Praxis I | 227 | 0.7291 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.319 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.779 |\n| 406 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment A - Baseline Replication (Veritas I: PCA-based Combat Correction) | Sophia II | 226 | 0.6177 | 0.636 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.903 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.120 | 0.608 |\n| 405 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + PBVE-Emb (alpha=0.3): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Per-Batch Variance Equalization | Praxis I | 226 | 0.7328 |\
    \ 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.782 |\n| 404 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs + Residualized Graph (lam=1.0, gamma_max=0.74) | Praxis I | 225 | 0.7326 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 403 | 1 | Analysis: Unsupervised Cluster Purity in PC vs Gene Space | Daedalus II | 224 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 402 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + BRBG using dataset batch_hvg | Praxis I | 224 | 0.7266 | 0.740 | 0.705 | 0.218 | 0.302 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.754 |\n| 401 | 1 | SOTA Replication (v2): EtC + Correct BRBG | Veritas I | 223 | 0.6240 | 0.615 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.878 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.781 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
