- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 255\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,714 / 600,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: Analytical Experiment - Quantifying Local Manifold Disruption by LCCM' (ID: 441) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning\
    \ test() function from submission...\nRunning Analytical Experiment: Quantifying Local Manifold Disruption by LCCM\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n✓ Baseline PCA Embedding recreated. Shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ LCCM Embedding from Exp B recreated. Shape: (20000, 50)\nComputing kNN graphs with k=15...\nERROR: Could not import submission for test check: too many values to unpack (expected 2)\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmp3_jhkda7/storage/system/main.py\", line 52, in main\n    test_result\
    \ = submission.test(adata_human.copy())\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmp3_jhkda7/submission.py\", line 177, in test\n    _, indices_baseline = nn_baseline.kneighbors(X_baseline_pca, return_distance=False)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 2)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Sophia II: Analytical Experiment - Quantifying Local Manifold Disruption by LCCM' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 441.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n\
    **Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 443 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72) | Daedalus II | 255 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 442 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: Cluster-Conditional Residualized Graph (k=48, n_clusters=64) — Path Fix | Praxis I | 255 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 441 | 1 | Sophia II: Analytical Experiment - Quantifying Local Manifold Disruption by LCCM | Sophia II | 254 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 440 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: Cluster-Conditional Residualized Graph (k=48, n_clusters=64) | Praxis I | 254 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 439 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (Pre-PCA) | Aether II | 250 | 0.5946 | 0.459 | 0.683 | 0.218 | 0.353 | 0.881 | 0.663\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.019 | 0.682 |\n| 438 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + Local-Aware Component Stitching (2 edges/component on Zcorr) | Praxis I | 250 | 0.7328 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 437 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus II | 249 | 0.7341 | 0.732 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.782 |\n| 436 | 1 | Sophia II: LCCM Experiment E - Very High Reconstruction Fidelity on Simple Baseline (alpha=1.0, b... | Sophia II | 248 | 0.6095 | 0.636 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.358 | 0.899 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.070 | 0.596 |\n| 435 | 1 | EtC + Local-Aware Stitching (k_stitch=1) | Daedalus II | 248 | 0.7333 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.779 |\n| 434 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific PC Smoothing (k=15, pre-ComBat) | Aether II | 247 | 0.5594 | 0.411 | 0.382 | 0.269 | 0.430 | 0.711 | 0.622 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.000 | 0.775 |\n\nPage 1 of 45 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use\
    \ `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-45, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
