role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 264\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,737 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: Replication - Embed then Correct (EtC) SOTA (Daedalus II - ID 378)' (ID: 450) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7346934304768249\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.780  iLISI:\
    \ 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.736436  NMI: 0.700563\n  Graph_conn: 0.972128  kBET: 0.744146  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991751\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 450\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the bug in the original submission. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 450) failed with a `KeyError: 'highly_variable'` error at line 102 of the submission.\n\nThe issue was in the preprocessing section where two separate AnnData copies were created for different processing paths (embedding path and graph path):\n- `adata_for_embedding_path` - for the EtC (Embed then Correct) pipeline\n- `adata_for_graph_path` - for the BRBG (Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph) pipeline\n\nThe code called `_get_hvg_mask()` only on `adata_for_embedding_path` (line 101), which sets the `highly_variable`\
    \ column in that object's `.var` DataFrame. However, on line 102, the code tried to access `adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable']`, but this column was never created for `adata_for_graph_path` since `_get_hvg_mask()` was not called on it.\n\n**Error Location:** Line 102 in original submission:\n```python\nhvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable']  # FAILS - column doesn't exist\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a call to `_get_hvg_mask()` for `adata_for_graph_path` to ensure the `highly_variable` column is properly set for both processing paths.\n\n**Fixed code (submission_v2.py, line 194):**\n```python\nhvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\nhvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path)  # FIX: Added this line\n```\n\nThis ensures both AnnData objects have the `highly_variable` column properly initialized before attempting to access it.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) was monitored using the `monitor_evaluation.py` script.\
    \ The monitoring confirmed:\n- The code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing (monitor timeout)\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- No KeyError or other exceptions occurred\n- The evaluation is taking longer to complete due to computational complexity, but the code is functioning correctly\n\n## Result\nThe submission now executes the complete EtC (Embed then Correct) SOTA replication pipeline without errors, successfully implementing:\n1. Normalization and log1p transformation\n2. Highly variable gene selection for both paths\n3. PCA embedding followed by Combat correction for the embedding path\n4. Batch-residualized balanced graph construction for the graph path\n5. Final output with corrected embeddings and graph structure\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata\
    \ as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# --- Helper functions (from Sophia I's SOTA or general Scanpy practice) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10: # Fallback if too few HVGs are found\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50,\
    \ random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    # Add small epsilon to diagonal for stability if BtB is singular\n    epsilon = 1e-8 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32) + epsilon, B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0):\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\
    \    Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    sse = np.sum((y - yhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n    y_center = y - np.mean(y, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    sst = np.sum(y_center ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n    r2 = 1.0 - (sse / sst)\n\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :]) # Apply gamma_j as column-wise scaling to Zhat\n    return Zcorr, r2, gamma_j\n\ndef _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=24, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    per_batch_meds = {}\n    all_meds = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size < 3: # Need at least 3 cells for meaningful median/NN\n            per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n            all_meds.append(1.0)\n            continue\n\
    \        k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size) # Ensure k is not larger than batch size\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        d_no_self = []\n        for i in range(idx.size):\n            di = dists[i]\n            gi = inds[i]\n            mask = gi != i # Exclude self-neighbor if present\n            di = di[mask]\n            if di.size == 0: continue\n            d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n        if len(d_no_self) == 0: med = 1.0\n        else: med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n        per_batch_meds[b] = med\n        all_meds.append(med if med > 0 else 1.0)\n\n    # Handle case where all_meds could be empty if all batches too small\n    if not all_meds:\n        ref = 1.0\n    else:\n        ref = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n        if ref <= 0: ref = 1.0 # Avoid division by\
    \ zero\n\n    scales = {}\n    lo, hi = clamp\n    for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n        if med <= 0: s = 1.0\n        else: s = ref / med\n        s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n        scales[b] = s\n    return scales\n\ndef build_balanced_knn_calibrated(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_calib=24, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0: return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    scales = _batch_distance_scales(Z, batches, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp)\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        q = quotas[b]\n        if idx.size == 0 or q == 0: continue # Skip if batch empty or quota is zero\n\
    \n        k_nn_batch = min(q + 1, idx.size) # Ensure k for NN is not larger than batch size\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_nn_batch, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_nn_batch, return_distance=True) # Search across all cells for neighbors in current batch\n\n        neigh_in_batch = idx[inds] # Global indices of neighbors from current batch b\n\n        scale_b = float(scales.get(b, 1.0))\n        for i in range(n): # For each cell i\n            # Neighbors of cell i, specifically from batch b's fitted NN model\n            g_global_idx = neigh_in_batch[i]\n            di_scaled = dists[i] * scale_b\n\n            # Filter out self-loops and truncate to quota\n            valid_indices = [k for k, val in enumerate(g_global_idx) if val != i]\n            g_filtered = g_global_idx[valid_indices][:q]\n            di_filtered = di_scaled[valid_indices][:q]\n\n            for j, d in zip(g_filtered,\
    \ di_filtered):\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d) # Ensure symmetry\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0 # Binary connectivities\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for EtC SOTA Replication ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: Replication - Embed then Correct (EtC) SOTA (Daedalus II - ID 378)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration based on Daedalus II's EtC SOTA (Archive #9, ID 378) ---\n    N_PCS_EMB =\
    \ 60 # For EtC embedding path\n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50 # For BRBG graph path (from Sophia I's SOTA)\n    # BRBG parameters from Sophia I's SOTA (ID 201)\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.75\n    lam_adapt = 1.0\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    k_calib = 24\n    clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n    random_state = 0 # Consistent random state\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Create copies for each path to avoid unintended in-place modifications\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy() # Graph path uses original preprocessing without EtC Combat\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Common to both paths, up to HVG) ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path) # Apply to both copies\n\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n\
    \    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) # FIX: Call _get_hvg_mask on graph path too\n\n    # Ensure HVG mask is correctly applied if not already\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_graph\n\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (Embed then Correct - EtC) ---\n    print(\"Initiating EtC Embedding Path...\")\n    # 1. PCA on normalized, log1p HVG data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_embedding = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"  Initial PCA embedding shape: {X_pca_embedding.shape}\")\n\n    # 2. Combat correction on the principal components\n    # Temporarily store PCA embedding in adata.X for combat to operate on\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_embedding,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n\
    \        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n\n    Z_emb_etc = temp_adata_for_combat.X # This is the final EtC embedding\n    print(f\"✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_etc.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path (Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph - BRBG) ---\n    print(\"Initiating BRBG Graph Path...\")\n    # Use original HVG data from adata_for_graph_path\n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n\n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n    print(f\"  BRBG initial PCA (on HVGs) shape: {Z_graph_initial_pcs.shape}\")\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs,\
    \ batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn_calibrated(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, k_calib=k_calib, clamp=clamp\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], # Retain original observation metadata for evaluator\n        var=adata.var[[]], # Retain original variable metadata for evaluator\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_etc},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_etc_sota_replication',\n            'baseline_parameters': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'etc_embedding': 'PCA -> sc.pp.combat on PCs',\n\
    \                'etc_n_pcs_emb': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'graph_source_preprocessing': 'normalize_total+log1p+hvg',\n                'graph_source_dim_reduction': f'PCA (n_comps={N_PCS_GRAPH})',\n                'graph_batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization',\n                'graph_type': 'Calibrated Balanced kNN',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_k_calib': int(k_calib),\n                'graph_clamp': list(clamp),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_lam_adapt': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_metric': metric\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances\
    \ output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: EtC SOTA Replication pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: Replication - Embed then Correct (EtC) SOTA (Daedalus II - ID 378)\nInitiating EtC Embedding Path...\n  Initial PCA embedding shape: (20000, 60)\n✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating BRBG Graph Path...\n  BRBG initial PCA (on HVGs) shape: (20000, 50)\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: EtC SOTA Replication pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\
    \nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/19a3029c-a40e-4556-b1af-b0a4d17f1ab8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 19a3029c-a40e-4556-b1af-b0a4d17f1ab8\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET\
    \ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 452 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=32, gamma_max=0.7 (k=48) | Praxis I | 263 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 451 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=96, gamma_max=0.6 (k=48) | Praxis I | 263 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 450 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Embed then Correct (EtC) SOTA (Daedalus II - ID 378) | Sophia II | 262 | 0.7347 | 0.736 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.780 |\n| 449 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.8 (k=48) | Praxis I | 261 | 0.7270 | 0.720 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.343 | 0.958 | 0.669 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.935 | 0.782 |\n| 448 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.7 (k=48) | Praxis I | 261 | 0.7255 | 0.721 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.327 | 0.958 | 0.671 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 447 | 1 | Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE | Daedalus II | 257 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 446 | 1 | Sophia II: Analytical\
