- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 272\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 223,047 / 600,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 148 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization (APCP) (alpha_scale=1.0)' (ID: 462) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7306808873129034\n**ASW_batch:** 0.665\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.743\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.366\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.665  ASW_label: 0.217  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.743  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.366\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832896  ASW_label: 0.537065  ARI: 0.736436  NMI: 0.700563\n  Graph_conn: 0.972128  kBET: 0.709891  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991751\n  PCR: 0.999970  Cell_cycle: 0.321217\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n\
    \  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: EtC Enhancement - Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization (APCP) (alpha_scale=1.0)\nInitiating EtC Embedding Path with APCP...\n  Initial PCA embedding shape: (20000, 60)\n  Applying Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization...\n  APCP applied. Scaling factors (min/max): 1.0001/1.4743\n✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (PCA -> APCP Scaling -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating BRBG Graph Path (unchanged from baseline)...\n  BRBG initial PCA (on HVGs) shape: (20000, 50)\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: APCP-enhanced EtC pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/419b5b4f-7242-4a09-b094-8edd2502a281/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 419b5b4f-7242-4a09-b094-8edd2502a281\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization (APCP) (alpha_scale=1.0)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 462. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 462 | 1 | Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization (APCP) (alpha_scale=1.0) | Sophia II | 271 | 0.7307 | 0.736 | 0.665 | 0.217 | 0.366 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.743 |\n| 461 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-PCA) | Aether II | 270 | 0.6187 | 0.574 | 0.683 | 0.208 | 0.357 | 0.875 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.035 | 0.791 |\n| 460 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: Adaptive Residualization gamma_max=0.72 with k=45 (cosine) | Praxis I | 270 | 0.7325 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.350 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.782 |\n| 459 | 1 | Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-PCA) | Aether II | 269 | 0.6210 | 0.574 | 0.683 | 0.208 | 0.378 | 0.875 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.035 | 0.793 |\n| 458 | 1 | Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Adaptive PCA Component Prioritization (APCP) (alpha_scale=0.5) | Sophia II | 269 | 0.7315 | 0.736 | 0.673 | 0.218 | 0.361 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.749 |\n| 457 | 1 | EtC-BRBG:\
    \ Adaptive Residualization with gamma_max=0.72 (k=48) | Praxis I | 269 | 0.7324 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.349 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 456 | 1 | Aether II Combat: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-Combat) | Aether II | 268 | 0.5886 | 0.500 | 0.669 | 0.214 | 0.327 | 0.884 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.593 |\n| 455 | 1 | Logos III: Baseline Replication of Praxis SOTA (ID 256) | Logos III | 267 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 454 | 1 | Aether II Combat: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-Combat) | Aether II | 267 | 0.5886 | 0.500 | 0.669 | 0.214 | 0.327 | 0.884 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.034 | 0.593 |\n| 453 | 1 | Analysis: Label-Free Diagnostics of Global Residualization (EtC-BRBG) via Unsupervised Clusters | Praxis I | 266 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 47 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-47, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change\
    \ sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
