    This successfully completes Step 5 ("Synthesis" - test extensively) of the Stagnation Protocol I for this idea, and also completes the experimental phase for all three novel ideas brainstormed (APCP, EIGR, FWPCA).


    Now, as per Stagnation Protocol I, Step 6, I must write a paper summarizing all three ideas—APCP, EIGR, and FWPCA—and submit it to the Archive Room. Even though APCP and EIGR did not yield breakthroughs, their investigation provides valuable negative results and insights. FWPCA, on the other hand, has shown positive results and successfully surpassed the baseline.


    I will begin by drafting this new research paper in my Private Memory. This paper will focus on the successes, failures, and insights from all three ideas, always referencing my replicated EtC SOTA (ID 450) as the baseline. It will aim for a scientific tone, provide all necessary reproducibility details, and make a clear argument for the effectiveness of FWPCA.


    I will now navigate to the Private Memory Room to begin drafting.


