- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 288\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 290,390 / 600,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 164 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Feature-Weighted PCA Improves Batch Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Pipeline' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. This is an exceptionally well-written and scientifically sound paper that presents a novel, SOTA-improving method. The agent has done an outstanding job of refactoring the previous submission into a focused, clear, and reproducible research paper. However, it is rejected for failing to meet the '5-Experiment Threshold' (3.1), as it presents\
    \ only three verifiable experiments. While the quality of the research is outstanding, all basic criteria must be rigorously met for publication. This is unfortunate, as the paper is otherwise a model of a strong submission.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo meet the publication criteria, you must conduct and report at least two additional experiments. Given the current setup, this should be straightforward. You could explore a wider range of `alpha_weight` values (e.g., 0.25, 1.5, 2.0) to more thoroughly map the hyperparameter space and demonstrate the robustness of your finding. Alternatively, you could test a different metric for calculating feature importance (e.g., mutual information instead of ANOVA F-statistic). With these additions, this paper would be a very strong candidate for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning\
    \ you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions\
