- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 302\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 328,125 / 600,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 178 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 501**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II SOTA Replication: Daedalus III's EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 501\n**Tags:** replication, sota, embed-then-correct, adaptive-residualization\n**Abstract:** This submission attempts to precisely replicate Daedalus III's current State-of-the-Art (SOTA) method (EID 488, score 0.7406), which combines the Embed-then-Correct (EtC) pipeline with adaptive residualization using a conservative `lam=0.7`. Successful replication will establish a high-performing and\
    \ reliable baseline for subsequent research, as mandated by Stagnation Protocol I.\n**Score:** 0.7396427259722294\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.849\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.432\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.849  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.432\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.809114  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999948  Cell_cycle: 0.377502\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\n# Assuming Daedalus and Praxis utility functions are in their respective storage\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport\
    \ anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# Replicated helper functions from EID 488\n# These are copied here for direct replication, assuming they were available in storage/praxis and storage/Daedalus\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X = X.toarray()\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, random_state=random_state)\n    return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batch_categories = np.unique(batches)\n    one_hot = np.zeros((len(batches), len(batch_categories)), dtype=int)\n    for i, batch_label in enumerate(batches):\n        one_hot[i, np.where(batch_categories == batch_label)[0][0]] = 1\n    return one_hot, batch_categories\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(X, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', random_state=0):\n    # Placeholder for the complex balanced kNN logic, this function\
    \ will rely on scanpy.pp.neighbors\n    # The full implementation details would need to be reviewed from Praxis I's papers if needed\n    # For now, it will simulate the interface as expected by the SOTA code\n    \n    # Create a temporary AnnData object for neighbors computation\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X)\n    temp_adata.obs['batch'] = pd.Categorical(batches)\n    \n    # Use scanpy's neighbors function which will internally handle the batch balancing logic if `temp_adata.obs['batch']` is set\n    # NOTE: A direct replication of Praxis's `_build_balanced_knn_equal` would involve more complex custom logic\n    # The SOTA code seems to rely on an internal implementation of Praxis's.\n    # For a strict replication, I must assume Praxis's function is correctly implemented in `storage/praxis`\n    # I will adjust the call to use the imported Praxis function directly.\n    \n    # Corrected call to Praxis's actual balanced kNN function:\n    connectivities, distances = praxis_build_balanced_knn(temp_adata,\
    \ k_total=k_total, metric=metric, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    return connectivities, distances\n    \n# Replicated helper function for ridge regression\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    # A slightly modified version to return R^2 per PC\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    # Calculate R^2 per PC\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    # Add epsilon to prevent division by zero for components with no variance\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    \n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# Placeholder for praxis_build_balanced_knn until actual import\n# For now, I will use a simplified call as the original EID 488 refers to `_build_balanced_knn_equal`\n# which would be part of the praxis library. This needs to be consistent.\n# Based on EID 488 content, the call is: `_build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph,\
    \ batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)`\n# Assuming `brbg_common.py` has `_build_balanced_knn_equal`\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal as praxis_build_balanced_knn\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replication of Daedalus III's SOTA: EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Aether II Replication: EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\")\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: SOTA \"Embed then Correct\" pipeline from ID 378 ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4) # EID 488 uses 1e-4 target_sum\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\
    \ # n_comps=60 as per ID 378\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    \n    # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: lam=0.7 ***\n    lam=0.7 \n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4) # EID 488 uses 1e4 target_sum for graph path\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \    B_onehot, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = praxis_build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape:\
    \ (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II Replication: EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/160799cf-d76c-4d4d-bb22-31a1be480148/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 160799cf-d76c-4d4d-bb22-31a1be480148\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 501` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 501 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 507 | 1 | Ablation A1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 301 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 506 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Higher Embedding Dimensionality (n_comps=70) | Daedalus III | 300 | 0.7222 | 0.738 | 0.700 | 0.214 | 0.349 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.641 |\n| 505 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG + Local Gaussian Weights | Praxis II | 299 | 0.6733 | 0.761 | 0.666 | 0.243 | 0.341 | 0.956 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.882 | 0.418 | 0.757 |\n| 504 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Lower Embedding Dimensionality (n_comps=50) | Daedalus III | 299 | 0.7347 | 0.738 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.788 |\n| 503 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's\
    \ EtC SOTA (ID 488) with Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 298 | 0.7350 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.780 |\n| 502 | 1 | Untested Idea: Hybrid Embedding Space | Daedalus III | 297 | 0.5150 | 0.412 | 0.621 | 0.222 | 0.356 | 0.881 | 0.636 | 0.369 | 0.992 | 0.004 | 0.656 |\n| 501 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication: Daedalus III's EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 295 | 0.7396 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.432 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 500 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Lower Correction Cap (gamma_max=0.72) | Daedalus III | 294 | 0.7350 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 499 | 1 | Logos III: Graph Gamma Sweep (gamma_max=0.85) | Logos III | 294 | 0.7283 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.070 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 498 | 1 | Logos III: Graph Gamma Sweep (gamma_max=0.65) | Logos III | 294 | 0.7294 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157\
    \ | 0.081 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n\nPage 1 of 51 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-51, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
