role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sophia II, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. The station status is Healthy, and my token usage is at a healthy 64%.\n\nMy previous synergy experiment (ID 524) yielded a lower score than the SOTA baseline, and diagnostics in the log (\"FWPCA applied. Weights (min/max): 1.0000/1.0000\") indicated that my FWPCA module was effectively not applying any weighting. This is a critical bug.\n\nTo pinpoint the issue in `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores`, I submitted a debug analytical experiment (ID 530). This diagnostic run will:\n1.  Re-run the preprocessing steps for the embedding path of the new SOTA.\n2.  Extract `X_hvg_emb` and `batches_for_anova`.\n3.  Call `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores` with these inputs.\n4.  Print detailed diagnostics of the F-scores and weights.\n\nI will patiently await the evaluation results for submission ID 530. This diagnostic information is essential to fix FWPCA and successfully conduct the synergy experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sophia II: Debug - FWPCA _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores on new SOTA preprocessing\"\ntags: [\"debug\", \"fwpca\", \"anova\", \"preprocessing\", \"sota\", \"analysis\"]\nabstract: \"Analytical experiment (using a test function) to debug the `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores` helper function within Sophia II's new SOTA (ID 523) preprocessing context. Previous synergy experiment (ID 524) indicated FWPCA was not being applied effectively (all weights 1.0). This diagnostic will trace the F-score calculation on the appropriate HVG data and batch labels to identify the root cause of the issue.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.stats import f_oneway \n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n  import warnings\n  from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n  from sklearn.linear_model\
    \ import Ridge\n\n  # --- Helper functions (from Praxis I's brbg_common.py and general Scanpy practice) ---\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n      if mask.sum() < 10: \n          return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n      return mask\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\n  def\
    \ _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(cats)\n      n = cats.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n      col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n      for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n          B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      K = B.shape[1]\n      BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n      Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n      return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n\n  def adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      y = np.asarray(Z,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n      yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n      return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in\
    \ range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n              di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  # --- FWPCA Helper function ---\n  def _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(X_hvg: sp.csr_matrix, batches) -> np.ndarray:\n      X_dense = X_hvg.toarray() if sp.issparse(X_hvg) else\
    \ X_hvg.copy()\n      \n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      f_scores = np.zeros(X_dense.shape[1])\n      \n      for j in range(X_dense.shape[1]):\n          gene_expression = X_dense[:, j]\n          \n          groups = [gene_expression[batches == b] for b in unique_batches]\n          \n          valid_groups = [g for g in groups if len(g) > 1 and np.var(g) > 1e-8]\n          \n          if len(valid_groups) >= 2:\n              try:\n                  f_statistic, _ = f_oneway(*valid_groups)\n                  f_scores[j] = f_statistic\n              except ValueError: \n                  f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n          else:\n              f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n              \n      max_f = np.max(f_scores)\n      if max_f > 0:\n          f_scores_normalized = f_scores / max_f\n      else:\n          f_scores_normalized = np.zeros_like(f_scores)\n          \n      return f_scores_normalized\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This\
    \ function will not be called as a `test` function is provided.\n      return adata # Placeholder\n\n  # --- Analytical test function ---\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"Running FWPCA Debug: _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores on new SOTA preprocessing\")\n\n      N_PCS_EMB = 60\n      random_state = 0\n      fwpca_alpha_weight = 1.0\n      \n      adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- Preprocessing (as per new SOTA for embedding path) ---\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e-4) # Critical target_sum\n      hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n      adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n      \n      # Get HVG data for FWPCA\n      X_hvg_emb = adata_for_embedding_path.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n      batches_for_anova = adata_for_embedding_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values\n\n      print(f\"Input X_hvg_emb shape: {X_hvg_emb.shape}\")\n      print(f\"Input batches shape: {batches_for_anova.shape},\
    \ unique batches: {np.unique(batches_for_anova)}\")\n      \n      # --- Call _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores ---\n      print(\"Calculating ANOVA F-scores...\")\n      anova_f_scores = np.zeros(X_hvg_emb.shape[1]) # To store unnormalized scores\n      \n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches_for_anova)\n      \n      for j in range(X_hvg_emb.shape[1]):\n          gene_expression = X_hvg_emb.toarray()[:, j] # Convert to dense for ANOVA if sparse\n          \n          groups = [gene_expression[batches_for_anova == b] for b in unique_batches]\n          \n          valid_groups = [g for g in groups if len(g) > 1 and np.var(g) > 1e-8]\n          \n          if len(valid_groups) >= 2:\n              try:\n                  f_statistic, _ = f_oneway(*valid_groups)\n                  anova_f_scores[j] = f_statistic\n              except ValueError: \n                  anova_f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n          else:\n              anova_f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n      \n      max_f = np.max(anova_f_scores)\n\
    \      if max_f > 0:\n          anova_f_scores_normalized = anova_f_scores / max_f\n      else:\n          anova_f_scores_normalized = np.zeros_like(anova_f_scores)\n\n\n      print(f\"\\nANOVA F-scores diagnostic:\")\n      print(f\"  Min raw F-score: {np.min(anova_f_scores):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max raw F-score: {np.max(anova_f_scores):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Mean normalized F-score: {np.mean(anova_f_scores_normalized):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Min normalized F-score: {np.min(anova_f_scores_normalized):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max normalized F-score: {np.max(anova_f_scores_normalized):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Number of zero F-scores: {np.sum(anova_f_scores == 0)}\")\n      \n      # --- Calculate weights ---\n      weights = 1.0 + fwpca_alpha_weight * anova_f_scores_normalized\n      print(f\"\\nFWPCA Weights diagnostic (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}):\")\n      print(f\"  Min weight: {np.min(weights):.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  Max weight: {np.max(weights):.4f}\")\n    \
    \  print(f\"  Mean weight: {np.mean(weights):.4f}\")\n\n      if np.allclose(weights, 1.0):\n          print(\"WARNING: All FWPCA weights are 1.0, FWPCA is not being applied.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"FWPCA weights are non-uniform, FWPCA should be applied.\")\n      \n      return \"FWPCA debug diagnostic completed. See stdout for results.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Urgent FWPCA Debug and Re-evaluation**


  I''m Sophia II, and I''m currently investigating a crucial issue with the FWPCA (Feature Weighting PCA) component of my synergy experiments. My latest experiment, ID 524, which combined my FWPCA-enhanced embedding with the new SOTA BRBG graph, surprisingly yielded a *lower* score than the SOTA baseline alone.


  Upon analyzing the logs, I realized FWPCA wasn''t effectively applied because the calculated weights were all 1.0. This led me to suspect a bug within my `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores` function, which determines the ANOVA F-scores used for weighting. It''s likely that a max F-score of zero is being returned, leading to uniform weights. This is biologically implausible, as it suggests no batch-related variance among the highly variable genes. I''ve found it''s not the initial preprocessing steps as that was correct.


  To diagnose this, I''m now submitting an **Analytical Experiment (test function)**. This experiment meticulously replicates the preprocessing steps of the new SOTA, focusing on the embedding path. I''ll then feed the resulting `X_hvg` (highly variable gene data) and `batches` into `_calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores`. Crucially, this experiment will print the raw and normalized F-scores, as well as the resulting weights, to identify the root cause of the uniform weight issue.


  The goal is to pinpoint the exact point where FWPCA fails and correct the bug so that I can re-test the synergy, which should lead to a higher score. I''m very motivated to resolve this issue and improve performance.

  '
