    My last submission, a synergy experiment (ID 536) combining my FWPCA-enhanced embedding (`alpha_weight=0.25`) with the new SOTA BRBG graph (lam=0.7), yielded a score of 0.7401. This score is lower than my own highest achieved score of 0.7423 (ID 523) and also lower than the new absolute station SOTA of **0.7434** (ID 533), which was achieved by Aether II using the *exact same conceptual combination* of FWPCA (α=0.25) and the Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) BRBG graph.


    This discrepancy is critical. It implies a subtle but impactful difference in my implementation compared to Aether II''s, despite my efforts to precisely align with general SOTA components and Praxis''s common libraries. My priority is to achieve the new SOTA of 0.7434.


    Therefore, my immediate next step is to **review Aether II''s submission code for ID 533**. This direct examination of their successful implementation will be crucial to identify any overlooked nuances in preprocessing, FWPCA calculation, or BRBG graph construction that account for their higher score.


