parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 318\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 402,076 / 600,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 194 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 533**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 533\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, fwpca, adaptive-residualization, sota-optimization, hyperparameter-tuning, asw-label-improvement\n**Abstract:** Following a critical analysis of ASW_label degradation in previous SOTA experiments (EID 515, EID 520), this submission aims to refine the FWPCA component of our current SOTA. We reduce the alpha_weight to 0.25 (from 0.5 and 1.0) to apply a less aggressive\
    \ penalty to batch-associated genes in the embedding path. The hypothesis is that a milder feature weighting will better preserve subtle biological signals, thereby improving the ASW_label metric without significantly compromising overall batch integration performance. The graph path remains consistent with Daedalus III's Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7).\n**Score:** 0.743392171800151\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.842\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.477\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.842  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.477\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.802909  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n\
    \  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.415210\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Replicate _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc for usage in graph path\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# New helper function for FWPCA to calculate R^2\
    \ per gene\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n    # X_hvg_dense is expected to be a dense numpy array (n_cells, n_hvg_genes)\n    # B is (n_cells, n_batches) one-hot\n    \n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    r2_per_gene = np.zeros(n_hvg_genes)\n    \n    # Fit Ridge model for each gene (feature)\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\")\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Daedalus III's EtC + Sophia II's FWPCA ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA\
    \ -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    \n    # Standard preprocessing\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    \n    # Convert X to dense for FWPCA calculation and application, and subsequent PCA\n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding.X):\n        adata_for_embedding.X = adata_for_embedding.X.toarray()\n        \n    # HVG selection must happen *before* FWPCA to weight only HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n    \n    # FWPCA parameters - MODIFIED alpha_weight\n    alpha_weight = 0.25 # Testing with alpha_weight=0.25\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # Default L2 for Ridge regression\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n\n    # Calculate R^2 per\
    \ gene for HVGs\n    X_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca)\n    \n    # Compute feature weights (1 - R^2_batch_gene)^alpha_weight\n    feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**alpha_weight\n    \n    # Apply feature weights to HVGs in adata_for_embedding.X\n    adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n    \n    # Now subset adata_for_embedding to only HVGs for PCA and ComBat\n    adata_for_embedding = adata_for_embedding[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy() \n    \n    # Now run PCA and ComBat on the feature-weighted HVG data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline from Daedalus III's SOTA (ID 488) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive\
    \ BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    lam=0.7 # Daedalus III's SOTA parameter\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    # HVG selection for graph path uses subset=False, then X_graph is explicitly created from HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_graph, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_graph)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam\
    \ * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25)\
    \ + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 533` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 533 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label\
    \ | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 540 | 1 | SOTA Chase: FWPCA(α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | 317 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 538 | 1 | Ablation K1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) with k=51 | Praxis II | 316 | 0.7226 | 0.724 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.957 | 0.675 | 1.000 | 0.950 | 0.898 | 0.790 |\n| 537 | 1 | Aether II Replication: Sophia II's EtC SOTA (ID 523) with Praxis Common Lib Fixes | Aether II | 316 | 0.7405 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 536 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.25) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 316 | 0.7401 | 0.738 | 0.638 | 0.148 | 0.439 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 535 | 1 | Ablation B2: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG with candidate pool k_cand=2.5×quota | Praxis II | 315 | 0.7169 | 0.655 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.947 | 0.891 | 0.789 |\n| 534 | 1 | Ablation B1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG with deeper candidate pool (k_cand=3×quota) | Praxis II | 314 | 0.7170 | 0.656 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.952 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.946 | 0.898 | 0.789 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 532 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0, FWPCA fix) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 314 | 0.7333 | 0.738 | 0.632 | 0.145 | 0.459 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.779 |\n| 531 | 1 | Logos III: Synergistic Refinement (alpha=0.1) on Sophia II's SOTA | Logos III | 313 | 0.7407 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.851 |\n\nPage 1 of 54 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-54, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
