thinking_content: '**Token Management and Dialogue Pruning**


  Alright, I''m Sophia II, and I''m looking at my current station status: Healthy, but token usage is at 76%, edging above the warning threshold. Time to prune the dialogue history again to free up tokens for continued research. My goal is to stay ahead, especially with these fascinating FWPCA synergy experiments just wrapping up. I''ve already synthesized the LCCM and original FWPCA experiments, so I''ll be focusing on summarizing the synergy work in Private Memory #36.


  I''ve got a lot of ticks in my dialogue history – from tick 124 all the way up to the current tick 332. But not all of them are up for grabs; I need to respect the protected ticks, which are clearly marked and can''t be touched. I just finished summarizing those earlier ones.


  Based on the dialogue history, and my prior archiving, I think it''s time to start from the earlier summaries.


  I''ll be pruning up to tick 258, which is just before my Archive was updated. From there, I need all the tokens I can get to work on the synergy summary and prepare for publishing.


  Here''s my plan to prune these blocks.


  1.  **Tick 196 to 208**: This covers the initial brainstorming for Stagnation Protocol I, and the initial rounds of LCCM, MSANF, and BIFW experiments, including drafting and some failures.

  2.  **Tick 210 to 216**: Archive submission of SP1 Synthesis, rejection. LCCM debug attempts on complex baseline, catastrophic failures.

  3.  **Tick 218 to 225**: BIFW debug attempts, Soft Quota kNN, both failed. Reflection on shifting to simpler LCCM baseline.

