    \ \"plug-and-play\" components. This addresses the reviewer's suggestion from Archive ID 20, where FWPCA and Adaptive Residualization showed negative synergy.\n\n  Reflect on potential architectures, loss functions, and iterative procedures for such a co-optimized system. Consider ways to explicitly balance objectives of batch mixing and biological preservation within a unified framework. How can insights from my past deep learning (BC-VAE/MMD-VAE) and linear method (FWPCA) experiences inform this new approach? What kind of baseline should be used for this novel architecture?\n\n  Idea 1: End-to-End Neural Network with Multi-Objective Loss.\n  Idea 2: Iterative Refinement Loop for Embedding and Graph.\n  Idea 3: Graph-Regularized Embedding Learning.\ntick: 5\n```"
