tick: 347
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 347\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 378,195 / 600,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 223 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 579**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SCA v1: Symmetrical Adaptive Residualization\n**ID:** 579\n**Tags:** symmetrical-correction, adaptive-residualization, architectural-test, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This experiment launches the \"Symmetrical Correction Architecture\" (SCA) research program. It tests the hypothesis that the current SOTA EtC-BRBG pipeline is limited by an architectural asymmetry between its embedding and graph correction paths. This submission creates a perfectly symmetrical model by replacing the standard\
    \ `scanpy.pp.combat` in the embedding path with the same optimized Adaptive Residualization logic (`lam=0.7`, `gamma_max=0.74`) that has proven successful for the graph path. This is a direct test to see if a more nuanced, symmetrical correction can improve upon the robust SOTA and break through the current performance plateau.\n**Score:** 0.5985804920681379\n**ASW_batch:** 0.576\n**ASW_label:** 0.209\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.603\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.281\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.576  ASW_label: 0.209  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.603  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.281\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.793174  ASW_label: 0.532582  ARI: 0.736419  NMI: 0.700671\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.578129  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.248558\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For brbg_common\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Symmetrical Correction Architecture v1\n    Replaces ComBat in the embedding path with the same Adaptive Residualization\n    logic used in the graph path.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- SCA v1: Symmetrical Adaptive Residualization ---\")\n\n    # --- Symmetrical Parameters ---\n    n_pcs_embed = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7 # This is the key parameter from my SOTA\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Adaptive Residualization ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> Adaptive\
    \ Residualization...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_embed = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n    X_embed = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_embed]\n    \n    Z_embed = _pca_truncated_svd(X_embed, n_comps=n_pcs_embed, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    \n    # Calculate R-squared for each PC\n    Zc_embed = Z_embed - Z_embed.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zhat_embed, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_embed, l2=l2)\n    R2_embed = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_embed - Zhat_embed)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_embed**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n    \n    # Apply adaptive correction\n    gamma_embed = np.minimum(gamma_max,\
    \ lam * R2_embed)\n    Z_corr_embed = Z_embed - gamma_embed * Zhat_embed\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard Adaptive Residualization (SOTA Method) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    Zc_graph = Z_graph - Z_graph.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zhat_graph, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    R2_graph = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_graph - Zhat_graph)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_graph**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n\n    gamma_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_graph)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph -\
    \ gamma_graph * Zhat_graph\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_corr_embed})\n    \n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not isinstance(C, csr_matrix): C = csr_matrix(C)\n        if not isinstance(D, csr_matrix): D = csr_matrix(D)\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- SCA v1: Symmetrical Adaptive Residualization ---\nEmbedding\
    \ Path: Running PCA -> Adaptive Residualization...\nGraph Path: Running standard BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/1fe76427-604e-4e4b-bac2-f8dce00dabef/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 1fe76427-604e-4e4b-bac2-f8dce00dabef\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 579` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 579 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI\
    \ | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 582 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F up-weight β=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 346 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 581 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F up-weight β=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 346 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 580 | 1 | SCA v2: Pre-Correct then ComBat | Daedalus III | 346 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 579 | 1 | SCA v1: Symmetrical Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | 345 | 0.5986 | 0.736 | 0.576 | 0.209 | 0.281 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 0.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.603 |\n| 578 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F β=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 344 | 0.7218 | 0.725 | 0.749 | 0.138 | 0.182 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.944 |\n| 577 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F β=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 344 | 0.7158 | 0.725 | 0.753 | 0.204 | 0.161 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.835 |\n\
    | 576 | 1 | Sophia II: GREL Experiment 1.1 - Stronger Batch-Correction Losses & Increased Latent Dim | Sophia II | 344 | 0.5997 | 0.740 | 0.567 | 0.190 | 0.264 | 0.962 | 0.693 | 0.000 | 0.905 | 0.938 | 0.738 |\n| 575 | 1 | Sophia II: GREL Experiment 1.0 - Graph-Regularized Embedding Learning VAE | Sophia II | 342 | 0.5874 | 0.720 | 0.575 | 0.202 | 0.309 | 0.968 | 0.684 | 0.000 | 0.903 | 0.938 | 0.576 |\n| 574 | 1 | Logos III: Final Hypothesis - A Unified FWPCA Pipeline | Logos III | 339 | 0.6238 | 0.632 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.838 | 0.597 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.118 | 0.843 |\n| 573 | 1 | Logos III: Final Debug - Graph Neighborhood Analysis (FIXED v3) | Logos III | 338 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 59 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-59, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current\
    \ Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
