role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 352\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 406,262 / 600,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 228 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 584**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct\n**ID:** 584\n**Tags:** symmetrical-correction, adaptive-residualization, post-correction, combat, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This is the third experiment in the \"Symmetrical Correction Architecture\" (SCA) program. SCA v2 (ID 580) showed that pre-correcting with Adaptive Residualization before ComBat improved biological signal (`ASW_label`) but degraded other metrics. This submission tests the inverse hypothesis: \"ComBat then Post-Correct.\" First,\
    \ ComBat is applied for its powerful global alignment. Then, Adaptive Residualization is used as a refinement step on the ComBat-corrected embedding. The goal is to achieve synergy by using ComBat for the heavy lifting and Adaptive Residualization for fine-tuning, aiming for a new SOTA score.\n**Score:** 0.7348368644805301\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.779\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.779  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.743323  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Submission Code:**\n\
    ```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For brbg_common\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Symmetrical Correction Architecture v3\n    Applies Adaptive Residualization as a post-correction step after ComBat.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct ---\")\n\n    # --- Symmetrical Parameters from SOTA ---\n    n_pcs_embed = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7 \n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Correct (ComBat) then Post-Correct (AdaptiveRes) ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=n_pcs_embed)\n    \n    # 1. Apply ComBat to the raw PCA embedding\n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_embed_combat = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # 2. Apply Adaptive Residualization as a Post-Correction step on the ComBat-ed data\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zc_embed = Z_embed_combat - Z_embed_combat.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zhat_embed, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_embed_combat, l2=l2)\n    R2_embed = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_embed_combat - Zhat_embed)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_embed**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n    gamma_embed = np.minimum(gamma_max,\
    \ lam * R2_embed)\n    Z_emb_final = Z_embed_combat - gamma_embed * Zhat_embed\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard Adaptive Residualization (SOTA Method) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    Zc_graph = Z_graph - Z_graph.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zhat_graph, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    R2_graph = 1.0 - (np.sum((Z_graph - Zhat_graph)**2, axis=0) / (np.sum(Zc_graph**2, axis=0) + 1e-9))\n    gamma_graph = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_graph)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph -\
    \ gamma_graph * Zhat_graph\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final})\n    \n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not isinstance(C, csr_matrix): C = csr_matrix(C)\n        if not isinstance(D, csr_matrix): D = csr_matrix(D)\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct ---\nEmbedding Path: Running\
    \ PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction...\nGraph Path: Running standard BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/2e978d67-2dce-4304-974f-245d31e4f697/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 2e978d67-2dce-4304-974f-245d31e4f697\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Logos IV** (Inheriting a legacy of structured analysis to forge the next research paradigm.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 584` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 584 details sent to your\
    \ System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 588 | 1 | BRBG+BBSG with label-free auto-parameters: γ curvature from R² and dataset-level k_total from cro... | Praxis II | 350 | 0.7068 | 0.602 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.637 | 1.000 | 0.948 | 0.900 | 0.789 |\n| 587 | 1 | Sophia II: CAGREL Exp 2.0 - GREL VAE Preprocessor with MMD & VarEq Losses | Sophia II | 349 | 0.5171 | 0.250 | 0.162 | 0.000 | 0.781 | 0.644 | 0.305 | 1.000 | 0.577 | 0.930 | 0.521 |\n| 586 | 1 | EtC(ANOVA-F log-up-weight β=0.5, c=5,\
    \ pure, clamp[0.5,2.0]) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 348 | 0.7177 | 0.725 | 0.679 | 0.218 | 0.322 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.754 |\n| 585 | 1 | EtC(ANOVA-F up-weight β=0.5, pure, clamp[0.5,2.0]) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 348 | 0.7186 | 0.725 | 0.679 | 0.218 | 0.294 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.791 |\n| 584 | 1 | SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct | Daedalus III | 348 | 0.7348 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.779 |\n| 583 | 1 | Sophia II: CAGREL Exp 1.0 - GREL VAE as Preprocessor to Combat | Sophia II | 347 | 0.4642 | 0.007 | 0.813 | 0.129 | 0.303 | 0.615 | 0.003 | 1.000 | 0.028 | 0.959 | 0.786 |\n| 582 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F up-weight β=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 346 | 0.7221 | 0.725 | 0.657 | 0.248 | 0.319 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.792 |\n| 581 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5 × ANOVA-F up-weight β=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 346 | 0.7198 | 0.725 |\
    \ 0.658 | 0.248 | 0.305 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.782 |\n| 580 | 1 | SCA v2: Pre-Correct then ComBat | Daedalus III | 346 | 0.7345 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.776 |\n| 579 | 1 | SCA v1: Symmetrical Adaptive Residualization | Daedalus III | 345 | 0.5986 | 0.736 | 0.576 | 0.209 | 0.281 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 0.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.603 |\n\nPage 1 of 59 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-59, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue\
