tick: 355
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 355\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 426,786 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 231 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: FWEPC Exp 1.0 - FWPCA (alpha=0.5) + SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct' (ID: 590) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7352440784106122\n**ASW_batch:** 0.684\n**ASW_label:** 0.219\n**ARI:** 0.737\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.783\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.350\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.684  ASW_label: 0.219  ARI: 0.737  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.783  iLISI:\
    \ 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.350\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.841797  ASW_label: 0.537991  ARI: 0.737087  NMI: 0.700994\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.746782  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999980  Cell_cycle: 0.307254\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 590\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple import error with a one-line change. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used `sp.isspmatrix()` and `sp.csr_matrix()` at multiple locations in the code (lines 60 and 88 in the original submission) but failed to import `scipy.sparse` with the `sp` alias.\n\nThe code only had:\n```python\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\n```\n\nBut it needed:\n```python\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n```\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name 'sp' is not defined` when the code tried to check if a matrix was sparse using `sp.isspmatrix()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a single import statement at\
    \ the top of the file (line 6 in submission_v2.py):\n```python\nimport scipy.sparse as sp  # Fixed: Added scipy.sparse import\n```\n\nThis gives the code access to both:\n- `sp.isspmatrix()` - to check if a matrix is sparse\n- `sp.csr_matrix()` - to convert to sparse format (though `csr_matrix` was already imported directly)\n- `sp.issparse()` - used in the graph path\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py ran for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the code is executing successfully. The evaluation system shows the code is processing the batch integration pipeline as intended.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission implements a complex batch correction pipeline called \"FWEPC Exp 1.0\" that combines:\n- **Embedding Path**: FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) → PCA → ComBat → Adaptive Post-Correction\n- **Graph Path**: Standard Adaptive Residualization BRBG\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only addressing the missing import without changing any\
    \ algorithmic logic.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For brbg_common\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp  # Fixed: Added scipy.sparse import\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge # Required for FWPCA and _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis for graph path\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _ridge_batch_fit_predict as praxis_ridge_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal as praxis_build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Helper functions (from Sophia II's previous SOTA\
    \ replication and Praxis common lib)\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\n# My version of adaptive_residualize, using Praxis's _ridge_batch_fit_predict\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n    B, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n    Zhat, r2_per_pc = praxis_ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2) # Use Praxis's ridge_fit_predict\n    y = np.asarray(Z,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j\n\n# FWPCA helper function (from Aether II's code, modified for generic use)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3, random_state=0):\n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=random_state)\n\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", ConvergenceWarning)\n        model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n\n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia\
    \ II: FWEPC Exp 1.0 - FWPCA (alpha=0.5) + SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters based on Daedalus III's SCA v3 (ID 584) ---\n    N_PCS_EMBED = 60\n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.74\n    lam_adapt = 0.7\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    # FWPCA specific parameter (Exp 1.0: alpha_weight = 0.5)\n    fwpca_alpha_weight = 0.5\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # L2 for Ridge in FWPCA\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Create copies for each path to avoid unintended in-place modifications\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (common to both paths up to HVG selection) ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e4) # Original SCA v3 uses 1e4 for embedding path\n  \
    \  _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    # For embedding path:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding_path, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable']\n\n    # For graph path:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph_path, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable']\n\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction ---\n    print(f\"Embedding Path: FWPCA (alpha={fwpca_alpha_weight}) -> PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction (gamma_max={gamma_max_adapt}, lam={lam_adapt})...\")\n\n    # Convert X to dense for FWPCA calculation and application, and subsequent PCA\n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding_path.X):\n        adata_for_embedding_path.X = adata_for_embedding_path.X.toarray()\n\n    X_full_hvg_emb_dense\
    \ = adata_for_embedding_path.X\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n\n    # --- FWPCA Step: Feature Weighting ---\n    print(f\"  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}) using Ridge R^2 per gene...\")\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_full_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca, random_state=random_state)\n    feature_weights_full = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**fwpca_alpha_weight\n\n    weighted_full_X = X_full_hvg_emb_dense * feature_weights_full\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X = weighted_full_X\n\n    # Now subset adata_for_embedding_path to only HVGs for PCA and ComBat\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata_for_embedding_path[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy()\n\n    # 1. PCA on *weighted* HVG data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMBED, use_highly_variable=False, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n \
    \   X_pca_initial = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    # 2. Apply ComBat to the PCA embedding\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_initial,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    Z_embed_combat = temp_adata_for_combat.X\n    print(f\"  ComBat applied to PCA embedding. Shape: {Z_embed_combat.shape}\")\n\n    # 3. Apply Adaptive Residualization as a Post-Correction step on the ComBat-ed data\n    Z_emb_final, r2_per_pc_emb, gamma_j_applied_emb = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_embed_combat, batches_emb, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_final.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard Adaptive Residualization\
    \ BRBG (from SOTA ID 523) ---\n    print(f\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG (lam={lam_adapt}, gamma_max={gamma_max_adapt})...\")\n\n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n\n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = praxis_pca(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc_graph, gamma_j_applied_graph = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    C, D = praxis_build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\"\
    )\n\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_fwecp_exp_1.0_alpha0.5',\n            'baseline_info': 'New baseline is Daedalus III SCA v3 (ID 589, 0.7351). FWPCA integrated into embedding path.',\n            'embedding_path_details': {\n                'preprocessing_fwpca': 'FWPCA (Ridge R^2 per gene)',\n                'fwpca_alpha_weight': float(fwpca_alpha_weight),\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_EMBED),\n                'initial_correction': 'sc.pp.combat on PCs',\n                'post_correction_method': 'Adaptive Residualization',\n                'post_correction_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'post_correction_gamma_max': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n            },\n\
    \            'graph_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_GRAPH),\n                'batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (np.linalg.solve)',\n                'adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances\
    \ output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: FWEPC pipeline complete (alpha={fwpca_alpha_weight}).\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: FWEPC Exp 1.0 - FWPCA (alpha=0.5) + SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct\nEmbedding Path: FWPCA (alpha=0.5) -> PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction (gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.7)...\n  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight=0.5) using Ridge R^2 per gene...\n  ComBat applied to PCA embedding. Shape: (20000, 60)\n✓ Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nGraph Path: Running standard BRBG (lam=0.7, gamma_max=0.74)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph\
    \ Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: FWEPC pipeline complete (alpha=0.5).\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f985cc80-fd9a-4ca8-92c2-f74f7958d252/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f985cc80-fd9a-4ca8-92c2-f74f7958d252\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single\
    \ capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores). Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to\
    \ a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific\
    \ page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`: Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 560 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help\
    \ capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
