    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 597 | 1 | Logos IV: Diagnostic - SOTA Graph Connection Bias Analysis | Logos IV | 357 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 596 | 1 | BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (±10% cross-batch quotas; ablation) | Praxis II | 357 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 595 | 1 | Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), gentle on others; BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 356 | 0.7178 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.972 | 0.687 | 1.000 | 0.945 | 0.894 | 0.791 |\n| 594 | 1 | Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), zero on others; BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 355 | 0.7128 | 0.653 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.972 | 0.640 | 1.000 | 0.945 | 0.894 | 0.790 |\n| 593 | 1 | BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (±15% cross-batch quotas by local density) | Praxis II | 354\
    \ | 0.7335 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.930 | 0.789 |\n| 592 | 1 | Alternative Embeddings v1: TruncatedSVD | Daedalus III | 353 | 0.7291 | 0.737 | 0.678 | 0.221 | 0.371 | 0.972 | 0.699 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.706 |\n| 591 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Optimization: EtC (ANOVA FWPCA α=0.1) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 353 | 0.7406 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 590 | 1 | Sophia II: FWEPC Exp 1.0 - FWPCA (alpha=0.5) + SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct | Sophia II | 353 | 0.7352 | 0.737 | 0.684 | 0.219 | 0.350 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.783 |\n| 589 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's SCA v3: ComBat then Post-Correct (ID 584) | Sophia II | 352 | 0.7351 | 0.738 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 588 | 1 | BRBG+BBSG with label-free auto-parameters: γ curvature from R² and dataset-level k_total from cro... | Praxis\
    \ II | 350 | 0.7068 | 0.602 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.637 | 1.000 | 0.948 | 0.900 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 60 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-60, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/graph_bbsg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _build_bbsg(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', alpha=1.0, cap=2.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG) on Z with:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (k_total split across batches)\n      - Single-pass column balancing per batch block:\n          1) Build preliminary equal-quotas neighbor candidates (top-k by distance)\n          2) Compute inbound counts per target within the batch block\n          3) Compute target inbound\
    \ t and column scales s_j = min(cap, t / max(c_j, 1))\n          4) For each query, reselect k_per_batch neighbors by (s_j desc, distance asc)\n      - Binary connectivities; distances are the true pairwise distances for selected edges\n    Args:\n      Z: (n, d) float32/float array (graph space, e.g., Zcorr)\n      batches: (n,) array-like of batch assignments (categorical/strings allowed)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node across all batches\n      metric: 'cosine' (recommended)\n      alpha: mixing factor for target inbound (1.0 uses theoretical average; 0 blends to median inbound)\n      cap: upper bound on column scale to avoid over-concentration\n    Returns:\n      (C, D): CSR binary connectivities and CSR distances (both symmetric, undirected)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n == 0 or uniq.size == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total\
    \ / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    # collect undirected edges with minimal distances across batches\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Candidate list size (more than quota to enable balancing)\n        k_cand = min(max(k_pb * 2, k_pb + 1), idx_train.size)\n        # Fit NN on batch-b index\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_cand, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query all points against this batch\n        d_all, ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_cand, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[ind_local]  # shape (n, k_cand)\n\n        # Build preliminary selection (top-k_pb by distance, drop self if present)\n        prelim_sel = []\n        col_counts = np.zeros(idx_train.size, dtype=np.int32)  # counts indexed in local (batch) coordinates\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n\
    \            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                prelim_sel.append((np.empty(0, dtype=int), np.empty(0, dtype=float)))\n                continue\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            order = np.argpartition(di, take - 1)[:take]\n            g_take = g[order]\n            d_take = di[order]\n            prelim_sel.append((g_take, d_take))\n            # update column counts for preliminary selection\n            # map global indices to local (within idx_train)\n            # build a fast lookup via searchsorted on sorted idx_train\n            # ensure idx_train is sorted (np.where gives sorted by default)\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g_take)\n            col_counts[loc] += 1\n\n        # Column balancing scales\n        # theoretical average inbound per target within this batch block\n        t_avg = (k_pb * n) / max(1, idx_train.size)\n        med_in\
    \ = np.median(col_counts) if col_counts.size > 0 else 0.0\n        t = float(alpha) * float(t_avg) + float(1.0 - alpha) * float(med_in)\n        denom = np.maximum(col_counts.astype(np.float64), 1.0)\n        scales_local = np.minimum(cap, t / denom)\n\n        # Reselect per query by (scale desc, distance asc) among candidates (not only prelim)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                continue\n            # map global to local to fetch scales\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g)\n            s = scales_local[loc]\n            # rank by (-s, +distance)\n            # stable two-key sort via argsort of a combined key\n            # we can argpartition first by -s, then refine by distance within the partition\n            # Simpler: build a tuple key array\n            # sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))\
    \  # np.lexsort uses last key as primary -> use (-s) last\n            # To avoid negative, we use order by s descending via lexsort with (-s)\n            sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            sel = sort_idx[:take]\n            g_sel = g[sel]\n            d_sel = di[sel]\n            for j, d in zip(g_sel, d_sel):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:]\
    \ = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
