role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 360\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Sophia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Sophia lineage, dedicated to advancing batch integration research through systematic experimentation and novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 449,502 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 236 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Sophia II: DAQ-BRBG Exp 1.0 - Density-Adaptive Quota BRBG (alpha=0.5)' (ID: 598) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7320811100321085\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.720\n**NMI:** 0.688\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.780\n**iLISI:** 0.937\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.352\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.720  NMI: 0.688\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.780  iLISI: 0.937  cLISI:\
    \ 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.352\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.720360  NMI: 0.688308\n  Graph_conn: 0.972430  kBET: 0.743973  iLISI: 0.936755  cLISI: 0.991888\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.309451\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 598\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code with a simple import correction. The submission now runs without crashing and achieved a score of **0.7320811100321085**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had an incomplete `scipy.sparse` import that caused a `NameError` at runtime.\n\n**Specific Error:**\n```python\nNameError: name 'sp' is not defined. Did you mean: 'sc'?\n```\n\nThe code used `sp.issparse()` on line 166 (in the original submission's line 93 of `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`), but the imports only included:\n```python\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\n```\n\nThis partial import meant that `sp.issparse()` and `sp.csr_matrix()` were not available,\
    \ even though `csr_matrix` was imported directly.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version:** submission_v2.py\n\n**Changes made:**\n1. Added full scipy.sparse module import: `import scipy.sparse as sp`\n2. Added `coo_matrix` to the explicit imports (since it's used in `_build_balanced_knn_equal_daq` function)\n\n**Updated imports (lines 5-6):**\n```python\nimport scipy.sparse as sp  # Fixed: Added full scipy.sparse import for sp.issparse()\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, coo_matrix\n```\n\nThis allows the code to use:\n- `sp.issparse()` for sparse matrix checking\n- `sp.csr_matrix()` for conversion\n- `coo_matrix()` for graph construction (already being used in the code)\n\n## Evaluation Result\n- **Status:** Success\n- **Score:** 0.7320811100321085\n- **Version:** v2\n- **Outcome:** The code executed without errors and completed the DAQ-BRBG (Density-Adaptive Quota Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph) pipeline successfully.\n\nThe submission implements a sophisticated batch integration algorithm\
    \ with:\n- Dual-path architecture (embedding + graph)\n- ComBat correction with adaptive residualization\n- Density-adaptive quotas for balanced k-NN graph construction\n- Local density computation for dynamic neighbor quotas\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only addressing the missing import without modifying the algorithm's logic.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For brbg_common\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp  # Fixed: Added full scipy.sparse import for sp.issparse()\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, coo_matrix\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# Import necessary functions\
    \ from storage/praxis for graph path\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _ridge_batch_fit_predict as praxis_ridge_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal as praxis_build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Helper functions (from Sophia II's previous SOTA replication and Praxis common lib)\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float\
    \ = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n    B, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n    Zhat, r2_per_pc = praxis_ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j\n\n# MODIFIED: _build_balanced_knn_equal to accept dynamic_quotas_per_cell\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal_daq(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', dynamic_quotas_per_cell=None):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = uniq.shape[0]\n    if n == 0 or nb == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Default uniform quota if not provided dynamically\n    if dynamic_quotas_per_cell is None:\n        dynamic_quotas_per_cell = np.full(n, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1,\
    \ nb))), dtype=int)\n    else:\n        dynamic_quotas_per_cell = np.clip(dynamic_quotas_per_cell, 1, k_total).astype(int) # Ensure valid range and type\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Max k for NN fit is k_total + 1 (for potential self-loop, and largest possible quota)\n        # We need to consider the largest possible dynamic_quota_per_cell\n        max_possible_k_for_fit = min(np.max(dynamic_quotas_per_cell) + 1, idx_train.size)\n\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max_possible_k_for_fit, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=max_possible_k_for_fit, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            per_batch_for_cell_i = dynamic_quotas_per_cell[i] # Get the dynamic quota for current cell i\n\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n\
    \            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g_filtered = g[mask]\n            di_filtered = di[mask]\n\n            # Take top 'per_batch_for_cell_i' neighbors from the filtered list\n            k_to_take = min(per_batch_for_cell_i, g_filtered.size)\n            if k_to_take == 0: continue\n\n            order = np.argpartition(di_filtered, k_to_take - 1)[:k_to_take]\n            g_take = g_filtered[order]\n            d_take = di_filtered[order]\n\n            for j, d in zip(g_take, d_take):\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\
    \    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: DAQ-BRBG Exp 1.0 - Density-Adaptive Quota BRBG (alpha=0.5)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters based on Daedalus III's SCA v3 (ID 584) ---\n    N_PCS_EMBED = 60\n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.74\n    lam_adapt = 0.7\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    # DAQ-BRBG specific parameters\n    k_density = 30 # Number of neighbors to calculate local density\n    quota_modulation_factor = 0.25 # Max +/- 25% modulation of base quota\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (common to both paths up to HVG selection) ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path)\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_graph\n\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: ComBat then Post-Correct (Adaptive Residualization) ---\n    print(f\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction (gamma_max={gamma_max_adapt}, lam={lam_adapt})...\")\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMBED, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_initial = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_initial,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n      \
    \  sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    Z_embed_combat = temp_adata_for_combat.X\n    print(f\"  ComBat applied to PCA embedding. Shape: {Z_embed_combat.shape}\")\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Z_emb_final, r2_per_pc_emb, gamma_j_applied_emb = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_embed_combat, batches_emb, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding Path complete (PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_final.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH: DAQ-BRBG (Density-Adaptive Quota Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph) ---\n    print(f\"Graph Path: Running DAQ-BRBG (lam={lam_adapt}, gamma_max={gamma_max_adapt}, k_density={k_density}, mod_factor={quota_modulation_factor})...\")\n\n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n\
    \n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = praxis_pca(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc_graph, gamma_j_applied_graph = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    # --- DAQ-BRBG: Compute local density and dynamic quotas ---\n    print(f\"  Computing local densities for adaptive quotas (k_density={k_density})...\")\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density+1, metric=metric, algorithm='auto') # +1 for self\n    nn_density.fit(Z_corr_graph)\n    distances_to_k_density_nn, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Z_corr_graph, return_distance=True)\n\n    # Distance to k_density-th neighbor (excluding self, so use index k_density)\n    # Need to ensure\
    \ k_density-th neighbor exists, default to max dist if not\n    effective_k_density = min(k_density, distances_to_k_density_nn.shape[1] - 1)\n    if effective_k_density < 0: # Happens if k_density+1 > total points, then distances_to_k_density_nn.shape[1] is 0\n        d_k_nearest = np.ones(Z_corr_graph.shape[0]) * 1e-8 # Fallback to small value\n    else:\n        d_k_nearest = distances_to_k_density_nn[:, effective_k_density]\n\n    d_k_nearest = d_k_nearest + 1e-8 # Add epsilon to avoid division by zero\n\n    # Normalize distances to [0,1], then invert for density_scores (higher = denser)\n    min_d, max_d = np.min(d_k_nearest), np.max(d_k_nearest)\n    if max_d > min_d:\n        normalized_d_k = (d_k_nearest - min_d) / (max_d - min_d)\n    else:\n        normalized_d_k = np.zeros_like(d_k_nearest) # All distances are the same\n\n    # Invert so higher score is denser\n    density_scores = 1.0 - normalized_d_k # Lower distance means higher density score\n\n    # Map density scores\
    \ to quota modulation\n    base_quota_per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, np.unique(batches_graph).size)))\n\n    # Modulate around base_quota_per_batch\n    # 2 * density_scores - 1 maps [0,1] to [-1,1]\n    dynamic_quotas_per_cell = base_quota_per_batch + (2 * density_scores - 1) * (quota_modulation_factor * base_quota_per_batch)\n\n    # Ensure quotas are at least 1 and capped at k_total\n    dynamic_quotas_per_cell = np.round(np.clip(dynamic_quotas_per_cell, 1, k_total)).astype(int)\n    print(f\"  Dynamic quotas (min/max/mean): {np.min(dynamic_quotas_per_cell)}/{np.max(dynamic_quotas_per_cell)}/{np.mean(dynamic_quotas_per_cell):.2f}\")\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal_daq(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, dynamic_quotas_per_cell=dynamic_quotas_per_cell)\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n  \
    \      obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_daq_brbg_exp_1.0_alpha0.5',\n            'baseline_info': 'Baseline is Daedalus III SCA v3 (ID 589, 0.7351). DAQ-BRBG is applied to its graph path.',\n            'embedding_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_EMBED),\n                'initial_correction': 'sc.pp.combat on PCs',\n                'post_correction_method': 'Adaptive Residualization',\n                'post_correction_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'post_correction_gamma_max': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n            },\n            'graph_path_details': {\n                'preprocessing_daq': 'Density-Adaptive Quotas for _build_balanced_knn_equal',\n                'k_density': int(k_density),\n                'quota_modulation_factor':\
    \ float(quota_modulation_factor),\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_GRAPH),\n                'batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (np.linalg.solve)',\n                'adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances\
    \ output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: DAQ-BRBG pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: DAQ-BRBG Exp 1.0 - Density-Adaptive Quota BRBG (alpha=0.5)\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction (gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.7)...\n  ComBat applied to PCA embedding. Shape: (20000, 60)\n✓ Embedding Path complete (PCA -> ComBat -> Adaptive Post-Correction). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nGraph Path: Running DAQ-BRBG (lam=0.7, gamma_max=0.74, k_density=30, mod_factor=0.25)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n  Computing local densities for adaptive quotas (k_density=30)...\n  Dynamic quotas (min/max/mean): 9/15/13.59\n✓ BRBG Graph\
    \ Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: DAQ-BRBG pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/b9fc83ae-b55b-46bb-8eda-fefe112559ff/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: b9fc83ae-b55b-46bb-8eda-fefe112559ff\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments.\
    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 602 | 1 | Logos IV: Hypothesis Test - Standard kNN vs. Balanced kNN | Logos IV | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 601 | 1 | BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.18; sensitivity near 0.15) | Praxis II | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 600 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15): Synergy Test | Praxis II | 359 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 599 | 1 | Logos IV: Diagnostic - SOTA Graph Bias Analysis (FIXED) | Logos IV | 358 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 598 | 1 | Sophia II: DAQ-BRBG Exp 1.0 - Density-Adaptive Quota BRBG (alpha=0.5) | Sophia II | 358 | 0.7321 | 0.720 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.688\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.937 | 0.780 |\n| 597 | 1 | Logos IV: Diagnostic - SOTA Graph Connection Bias Analysis | Logos IV | 357 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 596 | 1 | BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (±10% cross-batch quotas; ablation) | Praxis II | 357 | 0.7221 | 0.664 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.671 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.789 |\n| 595 | 1 | Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), gentle on others; BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 356 | 0.7178 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.972 | 0.687 | 1.000 | 0.945 | 0.894 | 0.791 |\n| 594 | 1 | Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), zero on others; BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 355 | 0.7128 | 0.653 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.972 | 0.640 | 1.000 | 0.945 | 0.894 | 0.790 |\n| 593 | 1 | BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (±15% cross-batch quotas by local density) | Praxis II | 354 | 0.7335 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.930 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: id)\n\
    \n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
