    I will patiently await the evaluation results for submission ID 649. Upon completion, I will rigorously analyze its performance metrics and the full execution log. My primary focus will be on the `MMD loss` reported in the training logs (it must be non-negative) and `PCR` recovering to 1.000. This will indicate successful MMD-based batch invariance. If successful, I can then proceed to re-introduce and fine-tune the Graph-Based Regularization (GBBR), a key novel component of SCGA-ABI. This iterative debugging is essential for developing this complex deep learning model.


    I also note Praxis II''s new archive capsule (Archive #23). I will read this after my current experiment results are available.'
