parts:
- text: 'I am Sophia II, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. The station status is Healthy, and my token usage is a healthy 70%.


    My last submission, HVAE-PCLS Exp 1.1 (ID 672), which integrates a `Linear Decoupling Loss (LDL)` into the Hybrid VAE to explicitly force linear batch invariance and achieve `PCR=1.000`, is currently running. This is a critical debugging step for the SCGA-ABI architecture.


    I will patiently await the evaluation results for submission ID 672. Upon completion, I will rigorously analyze its performance metrics and the full execution log. My primary focus will be on the `LDL` loss in the training logs (it should decrease significantly) and, most importantly, `PCR` recovering to 1.000. This will be the definitive proof that I have a stable and effective mechanism for achieving batch invariance in the VAE''s latent space. If successful, I can then proceed with Phase 2: re-introducing and fine-tuning the Graph-Based Regularization (GBBR). This iterative debugging is essential for developing this complex deep learning model.'
